(571, '2017-03-09 11:04:09', 89, 'Process, EMT', '', 'Email received from vendor as:\r\nThe calibration is fine. The power during the other processes is also fine.\r\nBy comparing 2 historicals, we can see that something happens at the beginning of the temperature ramp.\r\n \r\nDid the susceptor center using the outer quartz pins?\r\nDid the susceptor move during the process?\r\nIn these cases, the pyrometer 2 did not see only the susceptor but also the quartz window. And the pyrometer 2 temperature was wrong and the power increased.\r\n \r\nIf not, the BaF2 window (between pyrometer 2 and chamber) have to be checked.\r\nIf the BaF2 window is dirty, it has to be cleaned and the pyrometer calibration have to be checked after cleaning.\r\n\r\nAfter the calibration by controlling  the thermocouple kindly run the one recipe to check the calibration table. If there is not much variation in the power  we can run the recipe by using the pyro control.\r\n\r\nIf possible to clean the pyro window and  calibration please do it. I am ready to do that online guidance too. \r\nThe procedures  to cleaning of the pyro window  and calibration  document  is attached.\r\n \r\nHitesh is working on this', 'Hitesh, Pradeep', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '2017-03-10 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(563, '2017-03-09 11:05:05', 89, 'EMT, Process', '', 'EMT tried to install the files sent by vendor (Prof Arnone).\r\nBut there are some alarms coming.\r\nEmail sent to vendor for solution.\r\nWaiting for their response.', 'Sushil, Pradeep, Sarannya A', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
