(706, '2017-09-08 10:49:52', 89, 'EMT', '', 'As per vendor\\\'s suggestion, check was done. Following is reply from EMT side.\\r\\nPlease check the Pneumatic pressure switch inside the LPS, simply with an Ohmmeter\\r\\n> Checked... 1&3 open; 1&2 short; 4 is grnd.\\r\\nAnd please check the fuse.\\r\\n> We could not find any fuse. where it is located?\\r\\nDisconnect the bulb and check for a short circuit.\\r\\n> Hope this test is for LPS unit back side, in between anode & cathode. It is showing open\\r\\nWhen the Bulb is installed, the resistance between LPS and Lampsocket has to be less than 3Ohm.\\r\\n> with bulb connected, on the tool side connector, it is showing 5Mohm\\r\\nÂ \\r\\nDisconnect the LPS from any electrical power source before you open the cover\\r\\nPlease provide some photos from the opened LPS.\\r\\n> Photos attached.\\r\\nÂ \\r\\nÃ„Ã„Ã„HM the Lamp is in good condition? Can you try another bulb as well?\\r\\n> bulb is in good condition.\\r\\nIs the mercury in the bulb in one drop collected?\\r\\n> yes\\r\\nPlease suggest further checks.', 'Sushil, HiteshK', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', 'uploads/706_10.jpg', ''),
