(813, '2018-02-14 10:23:01', 89, 'EMT, Process', 'Tool software showing water flow error even though chiller manifold flow meter is showing 5 LMP flow.', 'Flushing of the water lines was done many times. Some algae came out while flushing, but after doing for 8-9 times, clean water is coming. \\r\\n\\r\\nAs per Raith engineer\\\'s suggestion, we checked the water flow sensor by disconnecting from the tool, it is working fine.\\r\\n\\r\\nWater connection to the tool is less as there is a common line from chiller to the tool & body.\\r\\nLate evening on Tuesday flow to the body was reduced and after that there was no water alarm in the tool.\\r\\n\\r\\nTool has been started by SO. Updates on the status of the tool will be given on Wednesday morning.', 'Bhimraj, Pradeep, Gayatri', 'Simco Global / Raith India', 'Mr. Pandurangiah.', 'Good', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(808, '2018-02-14 10:25:23', 89, 'EMT', '', 'While doing troubleshooting, found no issue in the tool. \\r\\nIf this occurs again, EMT will look into this.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn parallel, email about the issue has been sent to vendor.', 'Sushil', 'Om Scientific', 'Chintan Patel', 'Satisfactory', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(813, '2018-02-14 10:27:51', 89, '', '', 'As a long term solution, separate lines for the tool (GIS, turbo, electronics) and system body will be made.\\r\\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', 'For making new water connection, tool shutdown for half day is required. EMT & facility will co-ordinate with SO and decide on the dates'),
(706, '2018-02-14 10:28:52', 89, '', '', 'Lamp power supply is under repair with EVG, Austria.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(815, '2018-02-14 10:33:08', 89, 'EMT, Process', '', 'Issue was raised with the vendor. And the response is as below:\\r\\n\\r\\nFor your question, are you referring to like sharp corners with right angles? If this is so, I\\\'m sorry to say that this is a physic weakness in mask Aligner. This is due to light diffraction after the mask. However there is a way to solve this. May I know which exposure mode they use, vacuum contact? hard contact?\\r\\n\\r\\nIdeally we need to use vacuum contact for sharp feature. This is to minimize the diffraction to it lowest.', 'Pradeep, Hitesh K', 'Om Scientific', 'Chintan Patel', 'Good', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(815, '2018-02-14 10:33:59', 89, 'Process', '', 'Reply from our side:\\r\\nWe tried both contact mode i.e vacuum and hard contact. Seems in both contact mode gives edge roughness or not sharp corner.', 'HiteshK', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(815, '2018-02-14 10:35:04', 89, 'Process', '', 'New suggestion from vendor:\\r\\nThe straight lines are not sharp and have teeth-like features or lines are crooked. Many times, we have problems directly from the mask. Perhaps you may want to have a look at the mask under the microscope and see if the lines from the mask itself is â€œgoodâ€. Or maybe change a mask, especially SUSS Test mask if you have.\\r\\nTry the same recipe with suss test mask and see if you face the same issue.', 'HiteshK', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '2018-02-14 00:00:00', '', '', '', 'Hitesh K will do the test and revert back.'),
(782, '2018-02-14 11:28:28', 89, '', '', 'As per telephonic conversation, \\r\\nExcel Instruments will send the drawings and proposal by Thursday evening.', '', 'Excel Instruments', 'Mr. Raju / Mr. Pai', 'Satisfactory', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
