(769, '2018-06-05 10:42:24', 89, '', '', 'We have received the repaired Genius controller and Carrere unit from Ferrotec on 1st June 2018. Both the unit installation and cabling has been done today 4th June 2018.\\r\\nWe are waiting from facility side to complete the grounding as per suggested by vendor.\\r\\nAfter completion of grounding we will send grounding details and images to the Ferrotec for further action.\\r\\nNote :- As per Ferrotec suggested we have connected High voltage unit cable grounding to the chamber flange.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(883, '2018-06-05 15:21:19', 89, '', '', 'Heater Assembly and transformer sent to excel instrument for repair.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(887, '2018-06-05 17:21:57', 89, '', '', 'There was a small leak in pressure gauge adaptor which was connected to inlet cooling water line. The pressure gauge removed and the inlet cooling water line connected to tool.\\r\\nGauge is connected to check inlet water pressure purpose. (Not recommended)', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(885, '2018-06-05 17:25:07', 89, '', '', 'DP oil level is low. Top up the DP oil.\\r\\nAU update the status. Roughing & Backing vacuum 5E-02 mbar achieved in 7min is in spec. \\r\\nThere is no leak in the chamber.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(886, '2018-06-05 18:40:59', 297, 'Amit/Rajendra/Hitesh B/Irwin', 'Found Out Door Condenser Unit Contactor was stuck so compressor was not coming on. Hence lab humidity was high.', 'Checked the Lab dehumidifiers and emptied the water collected in them since morning - Hitesh B\\r\\nTrouble-Shooting Sequence: \\r\\n1] Checked Thermostatic Expansion Valve & concluded Comp 2 was not running\\r\\n2] Went out side and found Compressor 2 in idle condition\\r\\n3] Went up to unit power supply port and checked MPD found no alarm\\r\\n4] Checked contactor and found stuck. \\r\\n5] Replaced the stuck contactor with a functional one. \\r\\n6] Observed the data logger readings after making Comp 2 functional and found the humidity and temp came down within specs.', 'Rajendra, Amit, Irwin', '', '', '', '', 'One Contactor', 'NIL - was in spare', '0', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 'Keep monitoring Temp & Humidity, Check the Thermostatic Expansion Valves, Filter Dryer with Thermal Imager, Schedule the weekly wet cleaning of all the AHU condenser units within this week itself', 'Amit (Primary Owner), Irwin/Sandeep (Secondary Owners)', '', '1] 2 day shut down was taken over the last weekend to observe the behavior of temp & humidity under steady state conditions with no users in the lab. \\r\\n2] We observed that the dehumidifiers in the lab also throw hot air - hence they contribute to heat load and the fact that lab temp rises.'),
(879, '2018-06-05 18:52:29', 297, 'Amit/Rajendra/Hitesh B/Irwin', 'AHU power supply breaker in LT Panel tripped in the morning. \\r\\n\\r\\nIssue with heaters / heater contactor identified from trouble-shooting', '1] Went inside and checked all de-humidifiers to remove water but did not find any water collected - Hitesh B/Irwin\\r\\n2] Took shut down of AHU, checked heater bank contactors and found Bank 2 contactor has blue phase burn marks\\r\\n3] Isolated the blue phase outgoing cable from contactor to heater bank \\r\\n4] Also found one yellow phase outgoing cable to heater bank was not showing any power supply so traced it and remedied the situation by connecting it from another contactor of heater bank 1\\r\\n5] Physical checking of heaters done and also checked with multimeter and clamp meter. After checking the current draw of each heater some re-distribution was done across all the RYB phases\\r\\n6] 2 heaters found having issue (high current draw)so their power supply cable was isolated and kept tapped off\\r\\n7] Checked motor alignment, fitment to base frame and tightened all nuts & bolts again\\r\\n8] Blower/Impeller tightness checked again \\r\\n9] AHU started up and heater operation observed for no more power trips\\r\\n10] AHU has not tripped again since shut down completed', 'Facility Team', '', '', '', '', 'None', 'None', 'None', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '1] Weekly wet cleaning of condenser units to be scheduled\\r\\n2] Weekly check of condenser fan blade condition - if any crack is found - even minor - replacement will be planned \\r\\n3] Thermal Imager S', 'Amit (Primary Owner), Irwin/Sandeep (Secondary Owners)', '', '1] PM Shut Down is due for this AHU \\r\\n2] Electrical re-wiring of heater bank section proposed with separate mcb so if heater related issue comes only heater mcb trips not entire ahu. This way Blower & Compressor will continue running. There wont be too much spikes in Temp & Humidity then.'),
(878, '2018-06-05 18:56:46', 297, 'Rotex Air Con/Facility Team', 'Compressor has been replaced', 'Replaced the compressor but there was problem with HP Cut Out', 'Rotex/Facility Team', 'Rotex', 'Mr. Anand Bankar', 'Satisfactory', '', 'Compressor - 11 TR', '60,000/-', '3 - 4 Days', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '1] Weekly wet cleaning to be scheduled', 'Amit (Primary Owner), Irwin/Sandeep (Secondary Owners)', '', ''),
(857, '2018-06-06 10:01:49', 725, '', '1.periodic development and under development continuous throughout the written area. 100 um strip good development and followed by 100 um under development.\\r\\n2.Feature edges shows wave behavior, circles in design become ovals after development\\r\\n3. Developer got expired (MF 319)\\r\\n reasons:\\r\\n4.Development and under development might be due to laser beam non uniformity', '1. optimization of development time in Progress. DOE made after discussion with FIC. more details in attachment.\\r\\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', 'uploads/857_1.docx', ''),
(312, '2018-06-06 12:25:37', 89, '', '', 'Vendor have started identifying and rewiring of cables, etc.\\r\\nVendor have started the above work in his last couple of visit and did some more work yesterday.\\r\\nThe cabling work will take at least 4-6 more working days.\\r\\nThe work progress is bit slow because of vacation time however, Vendor want to speed it up in June.\\r\\nThey find it bit difficult carrying out thair work because of the space constraint and with all the dress code,etc.\\r\\nThey would like to take RF Power Supply to our work place for testing its control interface.\\r\\nThis is the reason we have deliberately postponed delivery of PO2 also.\\r\\nAdditionally once They deliver and bill to IITB they have to settle GST immediately in same month.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn 5th June vendor take out RF generator for testing purpose.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(816, '2018-06-06 12:49:47', 89, '', '', 'Purchase team had raised & approved indent (31st May 2018) for the procurement of RF generator as requested.\\r\\nPurchase team are in the process of raising inquiry for the same.\\r\\n', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
