(1323, '2022-12-02 15:27:49', 89, 'EMT', '', 'Repaired heater cable received from Excel Instruments on 1st Dec 2022\\r\\nContinuity test done on the repaired cable, to check for any short. No short found between the pins and the body\\r\\nHeater cable reinstalled on the system and following checks were done on 1st Dec 2022\\r\\n100deC â€“ 15mins\\r\\n200deC â€“ 15mins\\r\\n300deC â€“ 15mins\\r\\n400deC â€“ 15mins\\r\\n500deC â€“ 15mins\\r\\n600deC â€“ 15mins â€“ at this temperature, heater power connector at chamber side is getting warm. Not known if this is normal or not, as previous data does not exist\\r\\nHeater was powered down. And the cable connection was opened to see for any abnormal signs, like burning / carbon.\\r\\nNo abnormal signs seen', 'Vinayak', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(1323, '2022-12-02 15:29:31', 89, 'EMT', '', 'Following checks were done on 2nd Dec 2022\\r\\n700deC â€“ 15mins\\r\\n800deC â€“ 30mins\\r\\nAt these temperature, heater power connector at chamber side is getting warm similar to that at 600degC. Not known if this is normal or not, as previous data does not exist\\r\\nSystem has been kept in ideal condition with heater OFF', 'Vinayak', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
(1323, '2022-12-02 15:29:57', 89, 'EMT', '', 'Note: To confirm whether heater cable connector is getting warm is normal of not, we will be \\r\\nchecking the same in NMPF sputter at 800degC on Monday (5th Dec 2022)', 'Vinayak', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', '', '', ''),
