(1573, '2025-06-17 10:09:33', 297, 'AHU Chiller Team', '', 'Following Troubleshooting has been done:\\r\\nPrashant Removed the sensor from tank and check if alarm is going\\r\\nAlarm was still there even after rubbing the sensor on hand.\\r\\nRestarted the chiller again, PP alarm was still there\\r\\nThis indicate sensor is faulty and needs to be replaced.\\r\\nRaj informed MMIC and collected New Sub zero from Stores\\r\\nFaulty Temperature  Sensor from Chiller tank was removed \\r\\nNew  Temperature sensor was installed, Still PP alarm was there.\\r\\nChecked the cable – is there any cut or something.\\r\\nCross Checking of Sensor: connected the faulty sensor to New Sub zero and it read out temp as 31C\\r\\nIndicates Sensor is ok and cable is faulty. \\r\\n11. lay a new cable sensor from chiller tank to chiller panel. \\r\\n12. Chiller is working fine and PP fault is not there now', 'Prashant, Raj, Abhay, pawan', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
