(1676, '2025-07-07 10:23:26', 89, 'EMT', '', 'The chamber o-ring had removed from the slot.\\r\\nO-ring fixed back correctly and checked, chamber lid is getting closed completely now.\\r\\nReported issue is resolved', 'Pradeep', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Checked by Shahiroze'),
(1622, '2025-07-07 10:24:20', 89, '', '', 'This issue has been resolved by Mandar after connecting the DVD writer to the back side USB port of CPU\\r\\nChecked by Karuna', 'Mandar', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1621, '2025-07-07 10:26:04', 89, '', '', 'Mandar has connected a new DVD writer from stock\\r\\nChecked, now working fine\\r\\nReported issue resolved', 'Mandar', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Checked by Karuna'),
(1619, '2025-07-07 10:28:39', 89, 'EMT', '', 'The issue has been raised with OEM (Ultech)\\r\\nAction to be taken by EMT and discuss with OEM:\\r\\nTo find out the root cause of this issue\\r\\nSolution to be taken to avoid this iin future\\r\\nIs this expected? \\r\\nHow frequently chamber, showerhead cleaning is required?\\r\\nIs there any issue with gas line?', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1618, '2025-07-07 10:32:26', 89, 'EMT', '', 'Email sent to AJA for this issue.\\r\\nReply received, they are working on this issue and discussing internally with technical team. Will get back to us in this week.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn parallel, it is reported to Ferrotec also. Reminder email sent on July 7', 'Pradeep', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '2025/07/09', '', '', '', ''),
(1582, '2025-07-07 10:34:46', 89, 'EMT', '', 'June 25:\\r\\nTroubleshooting was done on this issue along with Oxford engineer online. They confirmed that the issue is with the PLC and suggested for an upgrade the PLC.\\r\\n\\r\\nEMT team (Pradeep, Avinash & Mandar) removed the PLC module and repaired it (heated the electronics components, PCB boards) and connected back to the system. Now the system is powered ON and kept under vacuum.\\r\\n\\r\\nToday the system will be kept in vacuum mode, tomorrow we can do a dummy plasma test run followed by a baseline run. \\r\\nIf all ok, the system can be opened for use', 'Pradeep, Avinash, Mandar', 'Oxford Instruments', 'Sateesh\\r\\nChandrasekhar', 'Satisfactory', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1582, '2025-07-07 10:35:38', 89, 'Process', '', 'June 27:\\r\\nReply from SO (Hemant) received that the plasma is not working due to chamber pressure not stabilized:\\r\\n\\\\ Today I have check system and try to do plasma chamber cleaning but system pressure gauge not stabilized due to which CF4+O2 plasma not generated. I have attached images & video for your refernce.Please look into it.\\\\', 'Hemant', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1582, '2025-07-07 10:37:04', 89, 'EMT', '', 'July 1:\\r\\nEMT worked on this further and below is the update sent to the stake holders:\\r\\nYesterday during troubleshooting, the PLC was found to be OFF and even with multiple tries, it did not start.\\r\\nSo EMT has replaced the faulty PLC with another from NCPRE.\\r\\nNow the tool is working and chamber pumped down is working fine.\\r\\n\\r\\nThere is issue with the process pressure. The actual value does not work with respect to the set value.\\r\\nWe will do further troubleshooting on this issue today and if required tomorrow also.', 'Pradeep, Avinash, Mandar', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '2025/07/07', '', '', '', ''),
(1582, '2025-07-07 10:39:42', 89, 'EMT', '', 'July 2:\\r\\nEMT worked on this further for the process pressure issue:\\r\\nDid procedure for the VAT controller as per manual sent by Oxford previously.\\r\\n1. Zero\\r\\n2. Learn procedure\\r\\n\\r\\nStill the issue is not resolved.', 'Pradeep', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'This issue needs to be reported to Oxford for further troubleshooting'),
(1582, '2025-07-07 10:40:26', 89, 'EMT', '', 'July 2:\\r\\nThe issue was reported to Oxford by email as below:\\r\\n\\r\\n We got old blue PLC from PECVD chamber from Prof Anil\\\'s lab as they have upgraded to new ones and installed the first two modules in the ICPCVD system.\\r\\nThe system is started now and in pumping stage \\r\\n\\r\\nBut when trying to run process run, the process pressure is not getting adjusted \\r\\n\\r\\nIn idle condition, the CM gauge fluctuates due to which penning gauge switches ON and OFF.\\r\\nPressure in the VAT PM-5 controller shows -14.5 mTorr whereas the software shows 0 mTorr\\r\\n\\r\\nWe tried doing learning procedure for the VAT, but still it is not working.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease let us know if we need to do some programming for the PLC?\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease help us find the cause of this issue and the ways to resolve this.', 'Pradeep', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1582, '2025-07-07 10:40:38', 89, '', '', 'July3:\\r\\nreminder sent', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1582, '2025-07-07 10:41:16', 89, 'EMT', '', 'July 3: \\r\\nReply received from Oxford (Chandrasekhar):\\r\\nThank you for reaching out to us with the detailed explanation.\\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nFrom the explanation it is evident that there is some offset between the APC and CM gauge. Which should have been resolved after your team reteach the APC. However, we would like to guide you remotely to re-teach the APC and see if we can resolve the issue. @Sateesh Kumar will remote support you today.\\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWe appreciate your understanding that the system is currently not under contract. However, we are pleased to provide you with remote support at no cost, reflecting our long-standing relationship. Should the need arise for an onsite visit, please note that there may be charges associated with that.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1582, '2025-07-07 10:48:18', 89, 'EMT', '', 'July 4:\\r\\nTroubleshooting on the issue was done with online video call support from Oxford engineer (Sateesh) on July 3 and July 4 full days.\\r\\nThe following work was done:\\r\\nWith NCPRE PLC, all the possible trials were carried out:\\r\\nVAT autolearning, config files checking, etc. But the issue of chamber pressure could not be resolved while striking the plasma.\\r\\nAlso the sample load / unload not working in manual mode.\\r\\n\\r\\nHence as suggested by Pradeep (EMT), old PLC was reinstalled after heating it up with hot air gun along with Mandar.\\r\\n\\r\\nSystem was restarted and chamber evacuation procedure done\\r\\n\\r\\nSample load / unload checked - working fine in manual mode\\r\\nPlasma strike checked - working fine for Ar, N2 till 1000W ICP & 30W RF\\r\\n\\r\\nSystem kept ON for monitoring for any issue', 'Pradeep, Mandar', 'Oxford Instruments', 'Sateesh', 'Satisfactory', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Further tests to be done on Monday (7 July 2025)'),
(1582, '2025-07-07 10:50:15', 89, '', '', 'Report sent by Oxford engineer is attached for reference', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/1582_9.pdf', ''),
(1591, '2025-07-07 15:08:45', 2457, '', 'Faulty XPS heat exchanger Di water pump repairing.', 'June 24 2025  \\r\\nOpened the faulty XPS heat exchanger Di water pump assembly and found out, that the  vanes which is placed in between the shaft is broken into pieces and because of this shaft was hardly moving, and we have to replaced the vanes with new one as the vanes was made from the graphite material and also graphite has high melting point.so we didn\\\'t have graphite material in our spares and as discuses with Chandrakant sir he had a graphite plates in his Workshop.  \\r\\n\\r\\nJune 25 2025\\r\\nSo, Chandrakant sir has some graphite plates in spares, So we measure the old vanes length, width, and height with vernier caliper and cut the graphite plate as measured and with the final touch-up placed the vanes (small cut graphite plates) in the shaft. So the problem of the vanes solved. but now we are facing new problem wit the bearing and the shaft.\\r\\n\\r\\nJune 26 2025\\r\\nLast time when started to assemble the XPS heat exchanger Di water Pump we got stuck with bearing and the shaft part, as pumps below side was assemble properly but top side having problem as the shaft is not going through bearing and we have to apply a bit of force to the bearing so the bearing can go through the shaft, but still shaft is not fully going into the bearing. so with the help of Chandrakant sir, will find some solution to it in the workshop.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1600, '2025-07-07 15:13:21', 692, '', '', 'due to moisture the water is coming and blower is off', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1510, '2025-07-07 16:06:05', 692, '', '', 'IR image taken done', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
