(1963, '2025-10-29 18:25:35', 2495, 'EMT', 'Actual value is not matching with set value.', 'As per the collected data the hot plate 3 \\r\\nThe average for 50°C the temperature recorded from the surface of the hot plate using external thermometer is 44.3°C (approx.).\\r\\nThe average for 100°C the temperature recorded from the surface of the hot plate using external thermometer is 92.2°C (approx.)\\r\\nThe average for 150°C the temperature recorded from the surface of the hot plate using external thermometer is 134.9°C (approx.)\\r\\n hot plate top surface is very dirty after cleaning EMT will recalibrate', 'Rhifa ,Vikas nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1962, '2025-10-29 18:29:53', 2515, 'EMT', '1. Hot Plate No. 2 is performing normally and stably.\\r\\n2. Temperate control and uniformity are within acceptable tolerance.', '1. Divided the Hot Plate surface into 3 rows & 3 columns using thermal tape to calibrate. \\r\\n2. Set the controller value temperature to 50°C. \\r\\n3. Set the controller value temperature to 100°C. \\r\\n4. Set the controller value temperature to 150°C.\\r\\n 5. All three set points (50°C, 100°C, 150°C) show small deviations within ±2°C. \\r\\n6. Heating uniformity across 9 sections is good.  \\r\\n7. Hot plate no. 2 is performing normally and stably.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad, Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/1962_0.pdf', ''),
(1931, '2025-10-30 09:54:25', 2515, 'EMT', 'We observed in the process chamber lid that the heads of two bolts were broken, which was causing a high vacuum issue.', 'We observed in the process chamber lid that the heads of two bolts were broken, which was causing a high vacuum issue. Then we placed a nut over the bolt heads and tightened them.\\r\\nSwitch on mains power supply (MCB), on the Chiller panel then turn the pump on the knob and turn on the compressor knob.\\r\\nSwitch on mains power supply (MCB) on the system.\\r\\nTurn on the power supply on the Rotary pump.\\r\\nThen Open the Roughing Valve and wait for the received 1.8E-2 vacuum (13 minutes).\\r\\nThen close the roughing valve and open the backing valve, reaching 5.0E-2 vacuum( 5 minutes).\\r\\nTurn on the turbo controller and reach for the full speed on the turbo pump (833Hz, 0.43Amp, 15 minutes).\\r\\nThen open the Gate valve (full) and wait for the reached 4.9E-6 vacuum(1 Hours 40 minutes ).', 'Pradeep Sir, Vikas, Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/1931_1.pdf', ''),
(1936, '2025-10-30 10:56:00', 89, 'Process', '', 'Update from SO (Mansi Patil) on Oct 28:\\r\\nThe vacuum has reached 6e-8 and Filament outgassing started today and will continue for approximately 2 days, and conditioning has started.', '', 'Icon Analytical', 'Tushar', 'Satisfactory', 'NA', '', '', '', '07-11-2025', '', '', '', 'NA'),
(1936, '2025-10-30 10:57:02', 89, '', '', 'Update from SO (Mansi Patil) on Oct 30:\\r\\nThe outgassing and conditioning is done.  Tushar will do calibration which will be done by tomorrow.\\r\\nWill update here when it is completed', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1904, '2025-10-30 11:00:21', 89, '', '', 'Oct 17:\\r\\nReplied to OEM, after cleaning the chamber, still same issue of \\\"High voltage minimum error\\\" seen\\r\\n\\r\\nOEM replied, we need to have a dummy plug to check if there is any issue with the CARRERA.\\r\\nAs IITB does not have it, Ferrotec will send a quote', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '30-11-2025', '', '', '', ''),
