(2079, '2025-11-27 09:56:54', 2457, 'EMT', 'DRIE SiC troubleshooting and trial run.', '* Sample wafer is in the process chamber. We first run \\\"Ox O2 clean/warmup\\\" recipe for 15 minutes. In O2 clean step, Table RF fluctuation seen - 32w, 9w, 16w, 25.9w, 31.4w, and He flow - 15 sccm, 8 sccm, 10 sccm, 12 sccm, 9 sccm. Then, we ran the \\\"Ox Sf6+O2 clean\\\" recipe for 15 minutes. Then, we run the purging recipe i.e. \\\"Ox Ar ESC Discharge-Purging\\\" for 10 minutes before opening the process chamber. After purging we vent the process chamber. Opened the process chamber to clean it with scotch brite and IPA. Cleaned the process chamber SS lid with scotch brite and IPA and also cleaned the top chuck where gases are introduced with scotch brite and IPA. Cleaned ceramic wall with IPA and Lint-free cloth. Removed the sacrificial ring and outer ring. Cleaned the sacrificial ring and outer ring\\\'s outer side and inner side with scotch brite and IPA. Cleaned ESC with lint-free and IPA. After cleaning the sacrificial ring and outer ring, fix it to its position. Then, pradeep sir checks the manual position of the sample wafer by\\r\\nClose the process chamber lid(to vent the L.L). Vent the L.L\\r\\n(Load the sample wafer in L.L\\r\\nOpened the slit valve manually i.e forcely. (to open the slit valve close both the chambers lid)\\r\\nExtend the arm.\\r\\nLead the ESC pins up.\\r\\nTake out the arm back.\\r\\nLead the ESC pins down.)\\r\\nKept the Sample wafer in the Process chamber. Put both the chambers in pumping. Will keep the process chamber pumping overnight.', 'Pradeep sir, Avinash and Anurag', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
