(1883, '2025-12-16 12:12:36', 297, '', '12th Dec Quote has been send for review to Deepti and Pradeep.\\r\\nReminder 1 has been send on 16th Dec by sandeep to both Deepti and Pradeep.                                                                                                              \\r\\n.                                                                                                                \\r\\n.', '.                                                                                                               \\r\\n.                                                                                                                         \\r\\n.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '31-12-2025', '', '', '', ''),
(2398, '2025-12-16 14:12:42', 279, 'EMT', 'After shower head cleaning, shower head fixed on the top side with Allan key screws. System power ON. Error showing on top heater controller display. Check the controller supply power cables. Thermocouple having issue', '1. Switch of the system.\\r\\n2. Again switch ON\\r\\n3. Same error on Top heater controller display\\r\\n4. Check the thermocouple connections all connected properly to the controller\\r\\n5. Removed thermocouple from the top side \\r\\n6. Checked thermocouple by using multimeter thermocouple gone bad.\\r\\n7. Thermocouple sample given to Mr.Jomon for new procurement\\r\\nOn 16/12/2025 reminder to Mr.Jomon for thermocouple', 'Vinayak', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2658, '2025-12-16 14:26:20', 279, 'EMT', '4 Target and Cr/Au evaporator shifted from micro 1 lab to EC lab by Mathadis. Request to facility team to connect the power cooling water and exhaust connections. once it will done EMT will clean the chamber and do a high vacuum test run', 'Cr/Au Evaporator\\r\\n1. Power, cooling water and exhaust connections done by facility team.\\r\\n2. Cr/Au Evaporator chamber cleaning by using IPA and lint free\\r\\n3. Chamber pumped down for high vacuum testing.\\r\\n4. High vacuum 4.5E-06 mbar reached in1 hour 10 minutes.\\r\\n\\r\\n4 Target\\r\\n1. Power, cooling water and exhaust connections done by facility team.\\r\\n2. By switching ON the system MCB burning smell coming out from PFIEFFER vacuum DCU 400 turbo controller.\\r\\n3. Main MCB off\\r\\n4. Turbo controller disconnected from the system.\\r\\nOpen the controller top cover, Varistor and two fuses gone bad.\\r\\n5. Email to Pradeep Nyaupane by Vikas for procurement', 'Vinayak, Vikas, Pradeep Nyaupane', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2662, '2025-12-16 14:38:04', 279, 'EMT', 'DC source not generating plasma. As we are setting power to 100W and turning on output it was not ramping up but showing value 0w.\\r\\nissue with the DC power source or with software mode remote or Local .', 'Back side panel opened to check the DC source. Cooling fan is working. Tightened all the power cables.\\r\\nchecked in system configuaration page\\r\\nPower-750W\\r\\nVoltage-1000V\\r\\nCurrent-1000mA\\r\\nbut still plasma not generating.\\r\\nChecked in system service page where max power for DC source showing value 0.This was reset to 750W and checked the plasma. Plasma generates and stable at 30mTorr & 3mTorr.', 'Vinayak, Hemant', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2662_0.jpeg', ''),
(2661, '2025-12-16 14:50:52', 2495, 'EMT', '1. we suspected that the IC in GVC2200 controller RS232 card is faulty hence the needed to try replacing it \\r\\n2. found MAX232 IC in spare \\r\\n                                                                                         .', '1. Found IC MAX232 in spare \\r\\n2. Took pictures of the controller panel , Vacuum controller , Software display before taking any action \\r\\n3. disconnected the GVC2200 controller by Disconnecting the ground, RS232, power cable, roughing and backing vacuum communication cable, Ion gauge vacuum communication cable, auxiliary power cable \\r\\n4. take out the GVC2200 controller and open the top and take out the RS232 card replace the IC and reconnect GVC2200 controller and checked and found that the issue is still the, the RS232 mode is not being selected', 'Rhifa, Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2589, '2025-12-16 14:52:22', 279, 'EMT', 'Nano litho Millipore DI water unit RO water tank which was kept in Nano lab service corridor back side.\\r\\nCheck RO water on weekly base it was observed that the RO water tank level is very low. Report to Mr. Pradeep', 'As per Mr. Pradeep refill the RO water tank with the help of housekeeping staff.\\r\\nCall to Chandrakant and Dinesh for the water filling.\\r\\nTake 20 litters bottle, filled DI water from wet chemistry lab and pour it into the RO water tank.\\r\\n100 litters DI water refilled in RO water tank', 'Vinaya, Chandrakant and Dinesh', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2482, '2025-12-16 15:08:40', 2495, 'EMT', 'The DI water dispenser in nano lab wet bench is showing resistance value between 15 and 16 Mega ohms                                                                                                                       \\r\\n                                 .', 'On 03 Dec Checked the DI water plant. Observed that the resistivity had further dropped to 13.7 Mega ohms.\\r\\nOn 04 Dec Display showed a prompt indicating Qgard and Quantum filters needed replacement. Sent a mail to inventory for both items.\\r\\nQuantum filter was not available in inventory, so a purchase request was raised. Further procurement process was handled by Vijay sir.\\r\\nReceived both the Qgard and Quantum on 10th Dec \\r\\nIssued a Qgard T1 and Quantum TEX from inventory \\r\\nThe step followed for replacement are as follows \\r\\nCleared the error by clicking the down arrow and then tick.\\r\\nPut the system into Standby mode and opened the Menu.\\r\\nNavigated to Maintenance Install Qgard.\\r\\nFollowed on-screen steps to remove the existing Qgard and replace it with the new one.\\r\\nExited Qgard installation using the Right arrow.\\r\\nSelected Install Quantum using the Left arrow and installed the new Quantum filter.\\r\\nReturned to main page and selected Ready.\\r\\nDispensed water to confirm both installations were successful.\\r\\nFlushed the system by dispensing minimum 25 litres of water, as white particles are normally observed after Qgard replacement.\\r\\nAfter that the system is ready to use   \\r\\nThe resistivity is back to 18.2Mega ohms', 'Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2303, '2025-12-16 15:10:11', 2495, 'EMT', 'The DI water dispenser in nano lab wet bench is showing resistance value between 15 and 16 Mega ohms rn                                                                                                         \\r\\n.', 'On 03 Dec Checked the DI water plant. Observed that the resistivity had further dropped to 13.7 Mega ohms.rnOn 04 Dec Display showed a prompt indicating Qgard and Quantum filters needed replacement. Sent a mail to inventory for both items.rnQuantum filter was not available in inventory, so a purchase request was raised. Further procurement process was handled by Vijay sir.rnReceived both the Qgard and Quantum on 10th Dec rnIssued a Qgard T1 and Quantum TEX from inventory rnThe step followed for replacement are as follows rnCleared the error by clicking the down arrow and then tick.rnPut the system into Standby mode and opened the Menu.rnNavigated to Maintenance Install Qgard.rnFollowed on-screen steps to remove the existing Qgard and replace it with the new one.rnExited Qgard installation using the Right arrow.rnSelected Install Quantum using the Left arrow and installed the new Quantum filter.rnReturned to main page and selected Ready.rnDispensed water to confirm both installations were successful.rnFlushed the system by dispensing minimum 25 litres of water, as white particles are normally observed after Qgard replacement.rnAfter that the system is ready to use rnThe resistivity is back to 18.2Mega ohms', 'Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2562, '2025-12-16 15:11:17', 2495, 'EMT', 'The DI water dispenser in nano lab wet bench is showing resistance value between 15 and 16 Mega ohms rn                            \\r\\n\\r\\n                                                                  .', 'On 03 Dec Checked the DI water plant. Observed that the resistivity had further dropped to 13.7 Mega ohms.rnOn 04 Dec Display showed a prompt indicating Qgard and Quantum filters needed replacement. Sent a mail to inventory for both items.rnQuantum filter was not available in inventory, so a purchase request was raised. Further procurement process was handled by Vijay sir.rnReceived both the Qgard and Quantum on 10th Dec rnIssued a Qgard T1 and Quantum TEX from inventory rnThe step followed for replacement are as follows rnCleared the error by clicking the down arrow and then tick.rnPut the system into Standby mode and opened the Menu.rnNavigated to Maintenance Install Qgard.rnFollowed on-screen steps to remove the existing Qgard and replace it with the new one.rnExited Qgard installation using the Right arrow.rnSelected Install Quantum using the Left arrow and installed the new Quantum filter.rnReturned to main page and selected Ready.rnDispensed water to confirm both installations were successful.rnFlushed the system by dispensing minimum 25 litres of water, as white particles are normally observed after Qgard replacement.rnAfter that the system is ready to use rnThe resistivity is back to 18.2Mega ohms', 'Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '');
INSERT INTO `trouble_track` (`complaint_id`, `timestamp`, `status_mark_by`, `working_team`, `diagnosis`, `action_taken`, `work_done_by`, `vendor_name`, `vendor_contact`, `vendor_interaction`, `vendor_comments`, `spare_parts`, `cost_spare_parts`, `procurement_time_spares`, `expected_completion_date`, `action_plan`, `action_item_owner`, `file`, `comments`) VALUES
(2040, '2025-12-16 15:17:09', 2495, 'EMT', 'The DI water dispenser in nano lab wet bench is showing resistance value between 15 and 16 Mega ohms rn                                                               \\r\\n                                      .', 'On 03 Dec Checked the DI water plant. Observed that the resistivity had further dropped to 13.7 Mega ohms.rnOn 04 Dec Display showed a prompt indicating Qgard and Quantum filters needed replacement. Sent a mail to inventory for both items.rnQuantum filter was not available in inventory, so a purchase request was raised. Further procurement process was handled by Vijay sir.rnReceived both the Qgard and Quantum on 10th Dec rnIssued a Qgard T1 and Quantum TEX from inventory rnThe step followed for replacement are as follows rnCleared the error by clicking the down arrow and then tick.rnPut the system into Standby mode and opened the Menu.rnNavigated to Maintenance Install Qgard.rnFollowed on-screen steps to remove the existing Qgard and replace it with the new one.rnExited Qgard installation using the Right arrow.rnSelected Install Quantum using the Left arrow and installed the new Quantum filter.rnReturned to main page and selected Ready.rnDispensed water to confirm both installations were successful.rnFlushed the system by dispensing minimum 25 litres of water, as white particles are normally observed after Qgard replacement.rnAfter that the system is ready to use rnThe resistivity is back to 18.2Mega ohms', 'Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2265, '2025-12-16 15:38:42', 2527, 'IT Team', '.                                                      test run for module modification                                                                                                                               .', '.                                                                                        testing completed                                                                                                                .', 'IT team', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2578, '2025-12-16 16:09:19', 726, '', 'During facility daily round, found ahu and lab pressure drop, and seen spike in lab temperature and humidity, the ahu pressure is drop from 50 mm of water to 40 mm water and lab pressure is drop from 6 mm of water to 4 mm of water.', 'During night shift staff daily round, lab pressure is drop and spike in temperature and humidity, inform in fic group and facility group, the reason pressure drop is ahu filter is chocked, send the ahu shutdown request to team head, further action will be taken after shutdown approval.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'AHU team had plan to shutdown the ahu for preventive maintenance (PM)'),
(2670, '2025-12-16 17:49:59', 2268, 'process', 'Shahiroze (2nd SO) had checked the gold display monitor and now it is showing correct values as per previous runs. She had also done the baseline runs before tool shifting and the tool is now working fine.', 'Shahiroze (2nd SO) had checked the gold display monitor and now it is showing correct values as per previous runs. She had also done the baseline runs before tool shifting and the tool is now working fine.', 'Shahiroze', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2672, '2025-12-16 18:00:08', 2527, 'Process', '.                                                         Lab condition is not suitable to run the process, due to process of renovation and drilling                                                   .', '.                                      The process run will be executed after 3 days of  multiple cleaning and restricted access.                                                                       .', 'work will be done by Gopika', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2673, '2025-12-16 18:03:19', 2527, 'Process', '.                                                         Lab condition is not suitable to run the process, due to process of renovation and drilling                                                   .', '.                                        The process run will be executed after 3 days of  multiple cleaning and restricted access.                                                                       .', 'Gopika', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2660, '2025-12-16 18:23:15', 2457, 'EMT', 'In software, CDA indication not turning into green indicating Interlock not satisfied.                                                                                                                          .', 'ICPRIE New \\r\\n\\r\\nSummary till now.\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Check the voltage supply of the CDA solenoid valve coil and it was showing 0vdc instead of 24vdc \\r\\n2. Check the relay supply to which the CDA solenoid valve coil is connected and it is also showing 0vdc.\\r\\n3. Checked the input supply of relay i.e. A1 and A2  terminal and it is showing 0 vdc.\\r\\n4. Checked the voltage supply of the CDA sensor and it was also showing 0vdc.\\r\\n5. Swap the N2 SENSOR 22.71 vdc supply to the CDA sensor.\\r\\n6. CDA sensor getting 22.77 vdc.\\r\\n7. In software cda does not turn into a green indication.\\r\\n8. While giving the N2 sensor 22 vdc, and turning On the PN2 valve, in software nitrogen turns into green.\\r\\n\\r\\nSuspected components are the:\\r\\n* CDA sensor to which cda is not indicating green.\\r\\n* Solenoid coil which is not turn on due to no voltage \\r\\n* Relay to check as it is not getting input supply of 24vdc.\\r\\n\\r\\nSolution:\\r\\nTo trace the connections of the input supply of  relay and cda sensor, I need help as all the connections lines are jumbled with other wires in the amount of small area.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1866, '2025-12-16 18:59:27', 1173, '', 'Test runs completed on Nano 2 RTP\\r\\n1) measured Native oxide\\r\\n2) N2 run for 180 sec, N2 900 sccm at 900 degree.\\r\\n3) O2 run for 180 sec, N2 900 sccm at 900 degree.\\r\\n4) Measured SIO2 thickness\\r\\ncomparative data is attached of Nano and Nano2 RTP and Nano \\r\\nSiO2 thcikness variation noticed in test runs between Nano and Nano 2 RTP.', 'After test runs with N2 and O2 to check SiO2 in both the runs in Nano RTP, it was suggested to repeat same runs with Nano 2 RTP to compare data. comparative data is attached of Nano and Nano2 RTP. SiO2 thcikness variation noticed in test runs between Nano and Nano 2 RTP.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/1866_5.docx', ''),
(2674, '2025-12-17 00:42:13', 2019, 'Prakash Mehra', 'Annex ground floor lab checking work ( micro-1, micro-2, wet chemistry lab, Nano gown area, Nano, Nano-litho lab,Nano-2 Nano UPS,) New building ground floor to 7th floor) checking safety device and violation.', 'Today night shift checking all annex side ground floor labs, Nano new building Mbe ground floor to 7th floor all corridor, safety device, and violation seen PPT prepread. please find the attachments below.', 'Prakash Mehra', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2674_0.pptx', ''),
(2675, '2025-12-17 00:45:27', 2019, 'Prakash Mehra', '1) Nano service corridor side GLD reading taken.<br />\\r\\n2.) 1.1 and 1.2 inside lab Smoke detector checking work.<br />\\r\\n3.) Safety blog,HR portal,Trouble shooting module update daily.<br />\\r\\n4.) CCTV camera monitor work.<br />\\r\\n5.) BMS desk duty.', '1.) Nano service corridor side GLD checking work done status update in safety portal device lsit section and also update google sheet.\\r\\n2.) 1.1 and 1.2 inside lab smoke detector checking work status update in safety portal device list.\\r\\n3.) All form are updated daily.\\r\\n4.) BMS desk duty and CCTV camera monitor work.', 'Prakash Mehra', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2669, '2025-12-17 09:30:49', 2495, 'EMT', '1. went and took the pictures of the system \\r\\n2. checked what are the connections \\r\\n3. went to the IITBNF website and downloaded the SOP of the system available there                                   .', '1. After downloading the Original SOP read and made notes\\r\\n2. Vinayak Sir helped in clearing any remaining douts related to system operation  \\r\\n3. Made an SOP for performing High Vacuum Test and shared it with Pradeep sir', 'Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2668, '2025-12-17 09:31:13', 2495, 'EMT', '1. went and took the pictures of the system \\r\\n2. checked what are the connections \\r\\n3. went to the IITBNF website and downloaded the SOP of the system available there                                   .', '1. After downloading the Original SOP read and made notes\\r\\n2. Vinayak Sir helped in clearing any remaining douts related to system operation  \\r\\n3. Made an SOP for performing High Vacuum Test and shared it with Pradeep sir', 'Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2129, '2025-12-17 09:46:43', 2378, '', 'Slot was postponded. Needs to reschedule after shifting work as Minita is busy.                            .                               .                                .                                   .', 'Slot was postponded. Needs to reschedule.                                           .                      .                  .                           .                    .                           .', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1860, '2025-12-17 12:15:54', 89, '', 'Quote received from vendor (Benchmark) of Rs. 56000\\r\\nProf Dipankar will speak to the vendor for cost negotiate                                                                                              .', 'After approval from team heads and FIC, 6nos of PC has been ordered and will be delivered by Nov 18 2025\\r\\nThe following is the plan:\\r\\n1. RTP\\r\\n2. HRXRD\\r\\n3. Olympus Microscope\\r\\n4. Slotbooking PCs 3  \\r\\n\\r\\nOnce these are received, windows installation and testing will be done for a week and them moved to the respective system', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '02-01-2026', '', '', '', ''),
(1995, '2025-12-17 12:22:54', 89, '', 'My network work group was used to transfer the data from System PC to another central location in the same IP domain\\r\\n                                                                                             .', 'The data transfer from system PC (lab tools) to another location which is accessible to all has been checked on few tools as per the below list:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. RTP system\\r\\n2. Dektak Profilometer Micro-2\\r\\n3. Dektak Profilometer 1.1\\r\\n4. Within slotbooking PCs\\r\\n\\r\\nTrial runs were done and one of the slotbooking PC was used as a central location for sharing files from different tools, and it is working. My network workgroup was used in this case having same IP domain in the network\\r\\n\\r\\nIssue faced: \\r\\n1. During check in HRXRD, it did not work with the existing system PC. We are planning to replace it with a new one in the near future. After this is done, the data transfer will be checked again\\r\\n2. The data transfer does not work for system PCs which have WinXP. Hence at present the Olympus Microscope, ICPCVD could not be checked.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis task will be completed by the 2nd week of January 2026.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '16-01-2026', '', '', '', ''),
(2564, '2025-12-17 12:28:35', 297, 'AHU Chiller Team', 'This complaint has been wrongly entered in NANO 1 AHU. we will be closing the complaint here as new complaint has been raised by anjum under NANO 2 AHU                                                                                   \\r\\n                                                                   .', 'This has been discussed with both anjum and Amit. that we will close the ticket and update the details in NANO 2 AHU ticket which is currently opened                                                                                  \\r\\n                                                                                                  \\r\\n\\r\\n.', 'Sandeep Mane', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1504, '2025-12-17 12:32:29', 297, 'Electrical Team', 'email has been send for procured on 3rd dec to purchase team. \\r\\nAll items has been approved by Team heads. waiting for purchase to happen                                                                                                     \\r\\n                          .', 'water pressure switch\\r\\nsub zero- MODEL- SZ-7510-P\\r\\nWaiting for the material to start the work \\r\\n\\r\\n....\\r\\n                                \\r\\n                                                                                                                          \\r\\n.', 'Sandeep Mane', 'Rajshree Electric', 'NA', 'Good', 'NA', '', '', '', '29-12-2025', 'once material is received, work will start', 'pintu', '', ''),
(1520, '2025-12-17 12:37:31', 297, 'AHU Chiller Team', 'waiting for Hexon chiller to deliver. once chiller is delivered and shut down dates are freeze we will get emd to work on this       \\r\\n.                                           \\r\\n.                                                                                        \\r\\n .', 'Tushar has been informed about the shutdown dates approx. 22nd to 24th dec and told to keep ac ready for installation work. Chiller will be delivered on Thursday and we need to get the plan for installation from vendor. Location of the AC will be change and we need to shift the extension board below the ACs		\\r\\n25 Nov 2025 11:18 AM\\r\\nAmit Kumar Das has per discussion with  ac EMD on ready to replaced both the ac in ppms lab , club with chiller installation work', 'Sandeep Mane', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '28-12-2025', 'Need to have checklist for the same', '', '', ''),
(1521, '2025-12-17 12:42:07', 297, '', 'on 10th dec\\r\\nHexon chiller guys have send email - Chiller will soon be ready for testing. I need some data so that we can factory fit the same.\\r\\nPlease confirm following\\r\\nWire length for remote controller from chiller.\\r\\nWire length of power supply\\r\\nReturn pipe OD\\r\\nAlso please ensure electrical wiring and connection as per last installed chiller. Supply pipe size is CPCV 1 ½”.', 'on 12 th dec sandeep has replied with details as per discussion with amit and prashant\\r\\nWire length for remote controller from chiller- 20 mts single length \\r\\nWire length of power supply- 23 mts single length\\r\\nReturn pipe OD= one inch', 'Sandeep Mane', 'Hexon', 'NA', 'Not Satisfactory', 'on 16th dec Hexon has replied on email for delay in delivery of chiller\\r\\nTo update you about delivery status of the PPMS chiller, system is ready and under testing.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will wind up testing by today day end and start finishing and packing dispatching process from very next day.\\r\\n\\r\\nSo we will dispatch system this Thursday or latest Friday.', '', '', '', '30-12-2025', 'we need plan of installation from vendor and dates on shutdown needs to be confirmed', 'prashant', '', ''),
(1753, '2025-12-17 12:45:05', 297, 'Electrical Team', 'Delay is there on this ticket due to the EC lab work. this activity is kept on hold for now. ECD 2nd week of Jan 2026.                            \\r\\n.                                                                                        .                                              \\r\\n                                                                                                                      \\r\\n.', 'Pintu to send out the material list for blowers.                                         \\r\\n                                                                                    \\r\\n   .                                                                                                        \\r\\n.', 'Sandeep Mane', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '15-01-2026', '', '', '', ''),
(2673, '2025-12-17 13:13:31', 2268, 'process', 'The baseline runs cannot be done because the EC Lab is not ready to do processes. Only tools are connected and the other things are pending. Once everything is arranged thorough cleaning will be done, only then the baselines can be conducted. As discussed in today\\\'s morning meeting the facility side clearance will be given by 6pm today. From tomorrow, further things will be carried out.', 'The baseline runs cannot be done because the EC Lab is not ready to do processes. Only tools are connected and the other things are pending. Once everything is arranged thorough cleaning will be done, only then the baselines can be conducted. As discussed in today\\\'s morning meeting the facility side clearance will be given by 6pm today. From tomorrow, further things will be carried out.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2673_1.jpg', ''),
(2672, '2025-12-17 13:14:27', 2268, 'process', 'The baseline runs cannot be done because the EC Lab is not ready to do processes. Only tools are connected and the other things are pending. Once everything is arranged thorough cleaning will be done, only then the baselines can be conducted. As discussed in today\\\'s morning meeting the facility side clearance will be given by 6pm today. From tomorrow, further things will be carried out. Kindly find the attached images of present lab for your reference.', 'The baseline runs cannot be done because the EC Lab is not ready to do processes. Only tools are connected and the other things are pending. Once everything is arranged thorough cleaning will be done, only then the baselines can be conducted. As discussed in today\\\'s morning meeting the facility side clearance will be given by 6pm today. From tomorrow, further things will be carried out. Kindly find the attached images of present lab for your reference.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2672_1.jpg', ''),
(2534, '2025-12-17 14:53:46', 726, 'AHU and chiller team', 'Water leakage observe in MBE 2 plasma source inlet water line, Issue flagged by student soumyadeep mukherjee on dated 10 december 2025 at 5:15 PM , who is system owner of MBE 2   .....................', 'Checked and identified the source of water leakage, closed the water line from manifold, Tight the nut ferule. observed that the water filter is also chocked, inform SO to replace the filter also, but due to out of stock filter, bypass the filter and run the system without filter, send procurement request by soumyadeep .Due to low pressure the interlock LED light is not glowing, requested by soumyadeep to increase the water pressure. increase the water pressure 1.8 bar to 3.8 bar after LED light is glowing and process resume.', 'Amit das', '', '', '', '', 'No', 'NO', 'NO', '', '', '', 'uploads/2534_0.pptx', 'Filter procurement request send by SO to MMIC.'),
(2634, '2025-12-17 17:33:55', 279, 'EMT', 'Observation by Anjum Ji, the ALD non LL water lines for the RF matching network getting brown color \\r\\nEMT observation the RF matching unit cooling water got brown color. Cooling water lines needs to be clean with IPA and high pressure CDA', 'ALD LL and non LL blackout done by Anjum\\r\\nALD non LL\\r\\nSystem shut down as per as per SOP\\r\\nCooling water line in/out valves closed from manifold\\r\\nRF matching unit cooling water lines disconnected from RF matching unit.\\r\\nBoth IN/OUT line cleaned with IPA and flushing done by high pressure CDA\\r\\nAll brown color remove.\\r\\nBoth lines connected to RF matching unit\\r\\nCooling water flushing done\\r\\nOpen IN/OUT valves system switched on as per SOP', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2634_0.jpeg', ''),
(2629, '2025-12-17 17:43:46', 279, 'EMT', 'Observation by Anjum Ji ALD LL RF matching unit cooling water lines getting brown color\\r\\nEMT observation the RF matching unit cooling water getting brown, request to Anjum Ji to black out the system, Both IN/OUT cooling water lines needs to be cleaned with IPA and flushing with high pressure CDA', 'System black out by Anjum\\r\\nSystem shut down as per SOP\\r\\nRF and turbo pump cooling water lines IN/OUT valve closed from the manifold\\r\\nRF matching unit cooling water lines disconnected and cleaned with IPA, flushed with high pressure CDA\\r\\nBrown color removed after cleaning two times\\r\\nBoth lines connected to RF and turbo pump\\r\\nSystem switched on as per SOP', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2629_0.jpeg', ''),
(2525, '2025-12-18 01:21:19', 690, 'Rajendra Khanvilkar', 'Complaint logged by Shilpa Kharat-04 Dec 2025-Complaint ID: 2356 in the equipment troubleshooting.<br />\\r\\nMulti-pocket Electron-beam Evaporator (4 target - GaN) Water leaking at the bottom side of the oerlikon system, kindly look into it.', 'First of all I went to the 1.1 inside lab oerlikon system and checked if there was any water leakage from the drain, after that I saw that there is issue in the pipe so first of all I heated the pipe with hot gun and after that I tightened the jubilee clip properly, now there is no water leakage from the system. please find the attachments below.', 'Rajendra Khanvilkar', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2525_0.jfif', ''),
(2376, '2025-12-18 01:26:57', 690, 'Rajendra Khanvilkar', '1.1 inside lab near passbox side Water leaking at the bottom side of the Oerlikon system, kindly look into it. \\r\\n1.1 inside lab near passbox side Water leaking at the bottom side of the Oerlikon system, kindly look into it.', 'First of all I went to the 1.1 inside lab oerlikon system and checked if there was any water leakage from the drain, after that I saw that there is issue in the pipe so first of all I heated the pipe with hot gun and after that I tightened the jubilee clip properly, now there is no water leakage from the system.', 'Rajendra Khanvilkar', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2376_0.jfif', ''),
(2666, '2025-12-18 09:52:34', 2515, 'EMT', 'I have downloded the THERMAL EVAPORATOR Cr/Au (Chromium / Gold) on the IITBNF website.                                                                                                                  .', 'Procedure\\r\\nSwitch ON the main MCB located on the right side of the system.\\r\\nSwitch ON the rotary pump by pressing the green push button on the main control panel.\\r\\nTurn ON the Pirani/Penning gauge controller.\\r\\nPR1 is displays the roughing vacuum.\\r\\nPR2 is displays the backing vacuum.\\r\\nSet the combination valve to the ROUGHING position and wait until the vacuum reaches 5.0E-2mbar.\\r\\nTurn ON the turbo pump and wait for speed it should be 1010Hz and power should be less then 10W.  \\r\\nAfter confirming stable turbo operation, set the combination valve to the BACKING position.\\r\\nThen slowly open the gate valve and then open it completely.\\r\\nWait for around 1 hour and 30 minutes, until the vacuum reaches 5.0E-6mbar. \\r\\n\\r\\nShutdown Procedure\\r\\nClose the gate valve completely.\\r\\nTurn OFF the turbo pump using the turbo pump controller and confirm that the pump speed has reduced to 0 Hz.\\r\\nSet the combination valve to the CLOSE position.\\r\\nTurn OFF the Pirani/Penning gauge controller.\\r\\n PR1 is Roughing vacuum\\r\\nPR2 is Backing vacuum\\r\\nSwitch OFF the rotary pump.\\r\\nSwitch OFF the main MCB located on the right side of the system.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2666_1.pdf', ''),
(2576, '2025-12-18 09:59:18', 2515, 'EMT', 'we have inspected the all communication wire, vacuum line connections and gas pipe connections.                                                                                                        .', 'Dismantled  the all communication cable with proper labelling. Dismantled the gas pipe connection.  Dismantled the vacuum line. All communication dismantled wire coiled with cable ties. Dismantled the vacuum oil pump. STSRIE system shifted from Micro Yellow room to Micro 2 lab.', 'Vinayak Sir, Vikas Kumar Nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2576_1.pdf', ''),
