(2671, '2026-01-01 17:07:32', 2268, 'process', 'Thermal Aluminium evaporator SOP has been updated. Additional images were attached in shutdown procedure. Reframed the procedure steps,and also added steps in deposition procedure and seperate headings for each are also added.', 'Thermal Aluminium evaporator SOP has been updated. Additional images were attached in shutdown procedure. Reframed the procedure steps,and also added steps in depostion procedure and seperate headings for each are also added.', 'Gopika Suresh', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2574, '2026-01-01 17:54:33', 2515, 'EMT & Process', 'Baseline run to be done by process team member SO Gopika ma\\\'am                                                                                                                                          .', 'The HRXRD tool relocation and re-installation in the MBE lab is completed. The baseline of the system after shifting is done using a standard Si wafer, and the tool is working fine. In addition to the baseline scan, I also carried out the other measurements like pre-rock and rocking curve analyses, XRR measurements for confirmation. Today, the vendor conducted an X-ray radiation leakage test. The detected leakage ranged between 0.09 µSv/h and 0.16 µSv/h, which is below the limit of 0.5 µSv/h, and it is safe to operate the system.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2574_1.pdf', ''),
(2769, '2026-01-01 18:01:32', 2515, 'EMT', 'After observing it was found that the metal O ring was lightly bended due heating to which it was not held on the chamber                                                                                 .', 'Opened chamber in presence of SO Shahiroze ji. Checked ‘O’ ring and lid found  that the metal O ring was lightly bent due to heating to which it was not held on the chamber. Replaced spare  metal ‘O’ ring and connected to the chamber, ‘O’ ring held on the chamber. Closed the chamber lid and tightened the bolt. System work done by the EMT side, informs SO Shahiroze Ji system will be checked and updated. SO Shahiroze ji checked the system and the updated system is working fine.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2769_0.pdf', ''),
(2842, '2026-01-01 18:02:50', 2515, 'EMT', 'After observing it was found that the metal O ring was lightly bended due heating to which it was not held on the chamber                                                                                                  .', 'Opened chamber in presence of SO Shahiroze ji. Checked &lsquo;O&rsquo; ring and lid found that the metal O ring was lightly bent due to heating to which it was not held on the chamber. Replaced spare metal &lsquo;O&rsquo; ring and connected to the chamber, &lsquo;O&rsquo; ring held on the chamber. Closed the chamber lid and tightened the bolt. System work done by the EMT side, informs SO Shahiroze Ji system will be checked and updated. SO Shahiroze ji checked the system and the updated system is working fine.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2842_0.pdf', ''),
(2271, '2026-01-01 18:28:55', 2515, 'EMT', 'Shahiroze (2nd SO) had checked the gold display monitor and now it is showing correct values as per previous runs. She had also done the baseline runs before tool shifting and the tool is now working fine.', 'Shahiroze (2nd SO) had checked the gold display monitor and now it is showing correct values as per previous runs. She had also done the baseline runs before tool shifting and the tool is now working fine.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2271_3.pdf', ''),
(2878, '2026-01-01 18:54:53', 2457, '', 'After PM of AHU and Chiller work was carried out by Facility team, tool was shutdown by Aquib ji, and after completing the PM when turned on the ICPRIE Old tool and open the VVV valve and throttle valve smoke leaked from the exhaust SS below of the process chamber pump.', '1.Changed the exhaust SS bellow with new one, so no more smoke leaked was observed.\\r\\n2. also it was observed rough vacuum or fine vacuum was not generating in the process chamber to which error pop up after every 5 minutes.\\r\\n3. checked the vacuum to the pump inlet side and it was 6.96E-3 mbar in 7 minutes.\\r\\n4. installed the new SS bellow and check the vacuum to the SS below mouth and it was 9.68E-3 mbar in 6 minutes.\\r\\n5. With the help of facilty team member raj insert the KF-40 SS below to 1.1 lab and installed it to ICPRIE process chamber and check the vacuum.\\r\\n6. Vacuum was stuck to 3.77E-1 mbar and 13.30 pa in baratron gauge.\\r\\n7.  Also, Turbo was not getting the cooling water flow to which we cannot turned on the turbo pump.\\r\\n8. So, facility member Raj increased the water flow from 4 bar to 5 bar, but no flow seen in turbo flow meter.\\r\\n9. close the water valve by raj and done the water line flushing of the turbo pump, and connected back its water line and open the water valves with 5 bar pressure.\\r\\n10. Now both ICP source and turbo getting cooling water.\\r\\n11. open the VVV rough valve and throttle valve and turned on the turbo pump.\\r\\n12. Turbo at full speed - 630Hz, current - 2.15A and Vacuum - 1.18E-3 bar in our controller.\\r\\n13. Kept the Process chamber pumping for overnight.', 'Avinash (EMT) and Raj (Facility)', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2864, '2026-01-01 18:58:17', 2515, 'EMT', 'Opening all the screws on the controller, I observed the fuse (6.3A/250V) and varistor (TVR 20431) was burned                                                                                               .', 'The faulty DCU controller was repaired successfully and the controller working condition. After testing turbo pump reached full speed 820 Hz, 1.06 and vacuum reached 1.2E-5mbar                            .', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad', 'Mr. Rajendra Sahu', '7337399345', 'Good', 'Vendor Mr. Rajendra Sahu suggested to buy the new controller.', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2864_0.pdf', ''),
(2848, '2026-01-01 18:59:23', 2457, '', 'water flushing the tool after Pm work done by facility team                                                                                                                                            .', '1. System was already turned off by the SO. 2. So after PM work of AHU and Chiller was complete, we started with the water line flushing. 3. Amit sir from facility turned off the inlet and outlet valves of the water line connection. 4. we removed inlet and outlet water line connection from ICP source side . 5. With CDA connection, apply cda flow to inlet side and water flush the line from tool side through outlet side. 5. Completed the water line flushing, told facility member Amit sir to open the both outlet first and then inlet water valves. 7. After water flushing, Aquib ji turned on the tool.', 'Avinash (EMT) and Amit ji (Facility)', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2703, '2026-01-02 12:17:07', 2465, '', 'Here is the observation of all clean rooms humidity and temp. In attached file there is testo data logger deviation data for clean room 31 Dec. in clean room there is some deviation seen in humidity and also in temperature.', 'Here is the observation of all clean rooms humidity and temp. In attached file there is testo data logger deviation data for clean room 31 Dec. in clean room there is some deviation seen in humidity and also in temperature. need to look into this .\\r\\n\\r\\nThis will review BY - Sandeep sir', 'Pawan kumar  sahu', '', '', '', '', 'na', 'na', 'na', '', 'This will review by Sandeep sir.', 'Pawan Kumar sahu', 'uploads/2703_11.png', 'Na'),
(2904, '2026-01-02 12:21:33', 2465, '', 'Here is the observation of all clean rooms humidity and temp. In attached file there is testo data logger deviation data for clean room 01 Jan. in clean room there is some deviation seen in humidity and also in temperature. need to look into this .', 'Here is the observation of all clean rooms humidity and temp. In attached file there is testo data logger deviation data for clean room 01 Jan. in clean room there is some deviation seen in humidity and also in temperature. need to look into this', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '31-01-2026', '', 'Pawan Kumar sahu', 'uploads/2904_0.png', ''),
(2863, '2026-01-02 12:32:23', 2495, 'EMT', 'after ahu and chiller pm work completed by facility team, did water line flushing of the tools                                                                                     \\r\\n                     .', '1. System was already turned off by the SO. 2. So after PM work of AHU and Chiller was complete, we started with the water line flushing. 3. Amit sir from facility turned off the inlet and outlet valves of the water line connection. 4. we removed inlet and outlet water line connection . 5. With CDA connection, apply cda flow to inlet side and water flush the line from tool side through outlet side.rn5. Completed the water line flushing, told facility member raj to open the both outlet first and then inlet water valves.rn7. After water flushing, hemant sir turned on the tool.', 'Rhifa, Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2867, '2026-01-02 12:40:22', 2495, 'EMT', 'after ahu and chiller pm work completed by facility team, did water line flushing of the tool                                                           \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n                                                                            .', '1. System was already turned off by the SO. 2. So after PM work of AHU and Chiller was complete, we started with the water line flushing. 3. Amit sir from facility turned off the inlet and outlet valves of the water line connection. 4. we removed inlet and outlet water line connection . 5. With CDA connection, apply cda flow to inlet side and water flush the line from tool side through outlet side.rn5. Completed the water line flushing, told facility member raj to open the both outlet first and then inlet water valves.rn7. After water flushing, hemant sir turned on the tool.', 'Rhifa , Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2846, '2026-01-02 12:58:29', 2495, 'EMT', 'after ahu and chiller pm work complete by facility team, did water line flushing of the tool pump                                  \\r\\n                                                                             .', 'Water inlet and outlet disconnected from the pump.\\r\\nHigh-pressure N2 purge in Inlet line.\\r\\nAfter N2 purge again water line flush with water.\\r\\nCleaned water flow sensor & switch.\\r\\nAfter flushing both inlet and outlet lines are connected to the pump', 'Rhifa ,Vikas nishad, Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2863, '2026-01-02 14:28:52', 2495, 'EMT', 'spinner found very dirty , resist was stick to the sides of the spinner     \\r\\n                                                                                                                       \\r\\n                                                                                                              .', '1. disconnected the spinner by disconnecting its vacuum and exhaust connections \\r\\n2. brought it to bms room \\r\\n3. opened the spinner top and removed the foil \\r\\n4. cleaned the sides using ipa, lint free cloth, scotch bright  \\r\\n5. opened the CDA lint port ad cleaned using IPA and lint free \\r\\n6.opened the spinner backside and cleaed the drain pipe \\r\\n7. reassembled the the spinner \\r\\n8. reinstalled it in Nano litho lab by connecting the power connection , exhaust line , cda line \\r\\n9. with help of hemant sir did a test run the spinner is working fine .', 'Avinash, Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2862, '2026-01-02 14:32:25', 2495, 'EMT', 'spinner found very dirty , resist was stick to the sides of the spinner \\r\\n\\r\\n                                                                                                                                             \\r\\n\\r\\n.', '1. disconnected the spinner by disconnecting its vacuum and exhaust connections .\\r\\n brought it to bms room . \\r\\nopened the spinner top and removed the foil . \\r\\ncleaned the sides using ipa, lint free cloth, scotch bright .\\r\\n opened the CDA lint port ad cleaned using IPA and lint free .opened the spinner backside and cleaed the drain pipe . reassembled the the spinner rn8. reinstalled it in Nano litho lab by connecting the power connection , exhaust line , cda line . \\r\\nwith help of hemant sir did a test run the spinner is working fine .', 'Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2657, '2026-01-02 14:40:30', 2495, 'EMT', 'After Facility connections done by facility team - power, exhaust\\r\\nCr/Au vacuum test was done\\r\\n                                                                                                                 \\r\\n                                                                                                         .', 'Time \\r\\nVacuum \\r\\nStatus\\r\\n\\r\\n11:02\\r\\n>1000 mbar \\r\\nRotary pump ON \\r\\n11:10\\r\\n8.6E +2\\r\\nRough valve ON \\r\\n11:14 \\r\\n5.0E -2\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n11:18\\r\\n3.9E -2\\r\\nBacking valve On\\r\\n11:19\\r\\n3.2E -2\\r\\nTurbo ON\\r\\n11:21\\r\\n2.6E -2\\r\\nTurbo in Full speed\\r\\n11:23\\r\\n2.2e -4\\r\\nGate valve open\\r\\n11:30\\r\\n5.0E -5 \\r\\nTurbo pump 1010Hz\\r\\n11:45\\r\\n1.8E -5\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n12:00\\r\\n6.9E -6\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n12:35\\r\\n4.4E -6 \\r\\nProcess chamber is is High vacuum \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4.4E -6 mbar high vacuum reached in 1 hour 10 mins', 'Rhifa, Vinayak', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
