(2936, '2026-01-05 18:42:11', 2457, 'EMT', 'MFC values fluctuation with VC412 controller                                                                                                                                                                    .', 'PDS Update \\r\\n\\r\\n1. Connected the Wi-Fi dongle to PC.\\r\\n2. Installed the new version of TeamViewer.\\r\\n3. Remote access with Pradeep sir.\\r\\n4. Transfer the new software zip folder to PDS PC \\r\\n5. Extract the zip folder and save it in mr.choi-jan 5 2026 new folder on Desktop.\\r\\n6. Before replacing it with an old folder.\\r\\n7. Went to C: -> program file x86 ->UPRO_SAH18011811\\r\\n8. Created backup-jan 5 2026 and copied all the 2019, 3 files in it.\\r\\n9. Open the mr.choi-jan 5 2026 folder and copy all the 2026 dated 3 files and paste it to the C: -> program file x86 ->UPRO_SAH18011811\\r\\n10. Now, C: -> program file x86 ->UPRO_SAH18011811 has all 2026 dated Files and application.\\r\\n11. opened the new updated software shared by ultech and checked the mfc values fluctuation.\\r\\n12. MFC value fluctuation is still there\\r\\n13. Observe issue email has been send to OEM.', 'Avinash and Pradeep sir.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2868, '2026-01-05 18:44:27', 2457, 'EMT and Facility', 'after the AHU and Chiller PM work completed by facility team tool water flushing has to be done.                                                                                                                                                              .', 'Tool water line flushing already has been done so told facility to only change the filter.                                                                                                                                                                                    .', 'Avinash and Raj', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(2863, '2026-01-05 18:59:30', 2457, 'EMT', 'servicing of nano litho lab PPR spinner.                                                                                                                                                                                .', 'After servicing of the spinner done by rhifa and vikas with cleaning of the sample holding chuck and vacuum valve by rhifa and removing of all the chock up resist from vacuum tube line connecting from sample holder chuck to vacuum valve by vikas. after cleaning all these things and reassemble of this things when connected the PPR spinner to Nano litho Lab it was still giving the Vacuum error i.e Vac=0 inhg. so, i take out the PPR soinner froom the lab take it to BMS room and again removed the sensor chuck where still resist was leaking, remove that part and clean it with lint free and IPA and also removed vacuum valve assembly and cleanit properly with IPA and lint free cloth and attached all the parts to its position and attached it to the spinner. and check the spinner in the presence of hemant sir and spinner worked properly with vac=21inhg.', 'Rhifa ,Vikas nishad and Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2863_2.jpeg', '');
