(2981, '2026-01-08 18:05:02', 2515, 'EMT', 'Inspected all cable connectors on the Olympus DP20 controller                                                                                                                                           .', 'Turn off the power button on the DP20 controller. Exit the Exit software on the PC and restart the PC. Turn ON the  DP20 controller.Refreshing the PC multiple and turning ON the software but error is still there. Again Turn off the power button on the DP20 controller. Remove all connected cable connectors and clean using IPA. Connected again cable connectors. Turn ON the DP20 controller. Refreshing the PC multiple times. Turning  ON the software but showing internal error: 0*2712  clicking ok and then clicking camera functions button the software. The system is going to Live mode and camera capturing the image. Inform Pankaj Sir to check the image. Pankaj Sir checked the image and the image was detected in the software. Pankaj sir Confirm the issue is resolved.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2981_1.pdf', ''),
(2976, '2026-01-08 18:08:37', 2515, 'EMT', 'Vacuum diaphragm pump issue                                                                                                                                                                                  .', 'In the presence of SO Mr. Hemant Sir, I have observed that there was a vacuum issue from the pump side. So we check the diaphragm pump which is placed in the Nano lab service corridor. The diaphragm pump did not create a good vacuum. To which we have changed its diaphragm and checked its vacuum.\\r\\nThen we removed the power cable and shifted from the Nano lab service corridor to the BMS room. Replaced the spare diaphragm pump with the DSA diaphragm pump and connected power cable in the diaphragm pump. In the presence of SO Hemant Sir, turn ON the system. Initializing the system. Load the mask and check the mask holder, now holding the mask . Issue resolved. Inform SO Hemant Sir for using the tool.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2976_1.pdf', ''),
(2975, '2026-01-08 18:10:32', 2515, 'EMT', 'Vacuum diaphragm pump issue                                                                                                                                                                               .', 'In the presence of SO Mr. Hemant Sir, I have observed that there was a vacuum issue from the pump side. So we check the diaphragm pump which is placed in the Nano lab service corridor. The diaphragm pump did not create a good vacuum. To which we have changed its diaphragm and checked its vacuum.\\r\\nThen we removed the power cable and shifted from the Nano lab service corridor to the BMS room. Replaced the spare diaphragm pump with the DSA diaphragm pump and connected power cable in the diaphragm pump. In the presence of SO Hemant Sir, turn ON the system. Initializing the system. Load the mask and check the mask holder, now holding the mask . Issue resolved. Inform SO Hemant Sir for using the tool.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2975_1.pdf', ''),
