(3138, '2026-01-14 12:57:17', 2268, 'Process', 'Lab cleaning done for nano, nano 2 , nano litho, Micro 2, and 1.1 and 1.2. Consumables refilled in MBE 2.', 'Lab cleaning done for nano, nano 2 , nano litho, Micro 2, and 1.1 and 1.2. Consumables refilled in MBE 2.', 'Gopika', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(3145, '2026-01-14 12:58:15', 2457, 'EMT and Oxford Engineers', 'DRIE maintenance visit by Oxford Engineers during Jan 12 - Jan 16 2026\\r\\n\\r\\nTroubleshooting for the following issues:\\r\\n1. Recipe not stable\\r\\n2. Wafer wobbling\\r\\n3. Table RF reflected power is not stable and sometimes high reflected power is seen\\r\\n4. He flow during process run is not stable. There is lot of fluctuations from (0.2sccm to 15sccm)\\r\\n5. Substrate alignment check\\r\\n6. N2 leak / high consumption\\r\\n7. Turbo pump water cooling pneumatic valve warranty replacement.', 'DRIE-SIC COBRA update.\\r\\nDay 2\\r\\nToday 13-01-2026\\r\\n\\r\\n1.	With Oxford engineers.\\r\\n2.	Stop process chamber pumping.\\r\\n3.	Stop load lock pumping.\\r\\n4.	Vented process chamber.\\r\\n5.	Started the lower side of the process chamber cleaning with new scotch brite, lint free clothes and IPA.\\r\\n6.	Chamber lid was already cleaned with scotch brite, Lint free clothes and IPA.\\r\\n                      \\r\\n7.	As process chamber low side was hard coated with the layers we use new Scotch brite.\\r\\n \\r\\n8.	Cleaned the low side of the process chamber with a small amount of ACETONE and new scotch brite and IPA. (We use little amount of ACETONE, because it may cause “O” ring to lose strengthens and take chamber a little bit more time for pumping).\\r\\n       \\r\\n9.	After cleaning the walls of the lower side of the process chamber with a bit amount force and circular way.\\r\\n10.	Cleaned the High vacuum gauge and capacitance nanometer gauge, keeping the chamber in atmosphere with lint free cloth and IPA and also cleaned the connected line with vacuum cleaner.\\r\\n11.	Again, cleaned the outer ring and sacrificial ring\\\'s inner side and outer side with scotch brite, IPA and Lint-free cloth.\\r\\n       \\r\\n12.	After cleaning, arranged the sacrificial ring and outer ring to its position and aligned the sacrificial ring properly with respective ESC.\\r\\n \\r\\n13.	Then, Oxford engineer manually check the position of the wafer with respective to ESC while both the chamber lid was opened.\\r\\n       \\r\\n14.	Tried this 2-3 times manually checking of the position of the wafer with respective to the ESC while both the chambers lid was opened.\\r\\n15.	After checking, set the alignment of the wafer and ESC fix and close both the lids.\\r\\n \\r\\n16.	Kept the chamber for pumping.\\r\\n17.	After lunch, we ran OX O2 clean/warmup recipe in sample wafer for 15 minutes. \\r\\n18.	No wobbling seen \\r\\n19.	Then, we vented the Load lock chamber.\\r\\n20.	And loaded plain sapphire wafer.\\r\\n21.	Ran Ox O2 clean/warmup recipe for 10 minutes.\\r\\n22.	No wobbling seen but wafer tilted little bit to left side.\\r\\n23.	Vented the Load lock chamber to Aligned the wafers position properly and then we run the actual recipe 3mtorr \\\"Ox SiC trial conductive clamping pre-stable\\\" recipe for 25 minutes.\\r\\n24.	No He flow and Table RF fluctuation seen.\\r\\n25.	We load back the sample wafer to Load lock to discharge it from the ESC.\\r\\n26.	 Again, put the sample wafer to the process chamber. (because, after etching ceramic wall of ICP is still remains in heated condition for some time and after getting cool down, flex or particles attached to the ceramic wall may get fall on the ESC, so that\\\'s why we load a dummy sample on the ESC to protects it from flex and particles).', 'Avinash, Oxford engineers and anurag', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3145_0.docx', 'Results: - after cleaning the lower side of the process chamber with new scotch brite and little bit of acetone and servicing of the high vacuum gauge and capacitance nanometer gauge recipe ran smooth with any fluctuation in He and table Rf.'),
(3157, '2026-01-14 13:01:16', 2268, 'Process', 'Lab cleaning done for nano, nano 2 , nano litho, Micro 2, and 1.1 and 1.2. Dead stock removal from each lab.', 'Lab cleaning done for nano, nano 2 , nano litho, Micro 2, and 1.1 and 1.2. Dead stock removal from each lab.', 'Gopika', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
