(3217, '2026-01-19 10:10:36', 2457, 'EMT', 'Helium leak and table RF fluctuation in 3mtorr recipe \\\"Ox SiC trial conductive clamping pre-stable\\\"                                                                                                                                                .', 'DRIE-SIC COBRA update.\\r\\nDay 4\\r\\nToday 16-01-2026\\r\\n\\r\\n1.	N2 cylinder replaced with the new one \\r\\n2.	ESC switching time changed to 10 sec from 8sec.\\r\\n3.	Ran \\\"Ox SiC trial 1 conductive clamping pre-stable with soft landing original\\\" recipe for 33 minutes, on dummy sample.\\r\\n4.	No wobbling seen.\\r\\n5.	Ran \\\"Ox Gan etch post SiC via etch\\\" recipe for 23 minutes.\\r\\n6.	He was 2-3 sccm and table RF was 2.8w.\\r\\n7.	No wobbling seen.\\r\\n\\r\\nPoints mentioned by Chandrakant sir (Oxford Engineer).\\r\\n•	The chamber needs to be clean with respect to the lower side wall of the chamber.\\r\\n•	The carrier wafer needs to be discarded after 2 runs as it should be not visible/transparent.\\r\\n•	Maximum 2 runs on carrier wafer. (Carrier wafer become thicker and thicker after each run it will cause helium to leak and can make C1 and C2 to tune again because of this reflected power will strike little bit high).', 'Avinash, Oxford engineers and anurag', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3217_0.docx', ''),
(3244, '2026-01-19 12:34:24', 279, 'EMT', 'LVPD precursor valve less space to operate.                                          .                    .', 'As per discussion with Nihal there is less space in the LVPD precursor. The precursor valve fitting is originally made by the company. We cannot do anything for this.', 'Vinayak and Nihal', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
