(3273, '2026-01-21 20:09:14', 95, 'Process Team', 'Sputter NMPF Al2O3 Target checked by opening main chamber. cleaned target surface with sand paper and load the target in the system', 'After reaching the vacuum at 1.5e-7 Torr Plasm striking check at 100W  RF powe plasma not strike. Al2O3 Plasma again checked at 150W RF it was working', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(3407, '2026-01-21 20:26:20', 2457, 'EMT', 'leak in Gas line check and gas box pneumatic check with high vacuum.                                                                                                                                                                                                       .', 'ICPRIE New update (21-1-2026)\\r\\n\\r\\nSummary:- \\r\\n* Block the gas line till the final valve i.e. high pressure diaphragm sealed valve  with female VCR fitting.\\r\\n* And check the leak, no leak observed till high pressure diaphragm valve.\\r\\n* MVV- 14.6Pa.\\r\\n* Turbo speed - 630 Hz\\r\\n* Current 1.25 A \\r\\n* Penning gauge- 1.48E-5mbar.\\r\\n\\r\\nToday update.\\r\\n* Reconnected the block section of the gas line to the high pressure diaphragm valve.\\r\\n* Open the VVV valve and throttle valve and check the MVV (foreline valve) pressure.\\r\\n* MVV pressure is 24.8 Pa which is good pressure compared to last time i.e. 580.3 Pa.\\r\\n* Try to open the VGQ valve but an error pops up.\\r\\n* Click on Ok.\\r\\n* Open the PN2 valve.\\r\\n* Turned ON the turbo pump.\\r\\n* Turbo at full speed - 630Hz.\\r\\n* Current - 1.04A\\r\\n* Penning gauge - 1.50E-5 mbar.\\r\\n* Turn off the turbo.', 'Avinash and Pradeep sir.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3407_0.docx', 'Further plan is to keep the process chamber for pumping and observe its vacuum and pressure.'),
(3052, '2026-01-21 20:29:50', 2457, 'EMT', 'leak in Gas line check and gas box pneumatic check with high vacuum.                                                                                                               .', 'ICPRIE New update (21-1-2026)\\r\\n\\r\\nSummary:- \\r\\n* Block the gas line till the final valve i.e. high pressure diaphragm sealed valve  with female VCR fitting.\\r\\n* And check the leak, no leak observed till high pressure diaphragm valve.\\r\\n* MVV- 14.6Pa.\\r\\n* Turbo speed - 630 Hz\\r\\n* Current 1.25 A \\r\\n* Penning gauge- 1.48E-5mbar.\\r\\n\\r\\nToday update.\\r\\n* Reconnected the block section of the gas line to the high pressure diaphragm valve.\\r\\n* Open the VVV valve and throttle valve and check the MVV (foreline valve) pressure.\\r\\n* MVV pressure is 24.8 Pa which is good pressure compared to last time i.e. 580.3 Pa.\\r\\n* Try to open the VGQ valve but an error pops up.\\r\\n* Click on Ok.\\r\\n* Open the PN2 valve.\\r\\n* Turned ON the turbo pump.\\r\\n* Turbo at full speed - 630Hz.\\r\\n* Current - 1.04A\\r\\n* Penning gauge - 1.50E-5 mbar.\\r\\n* Turn off the turbo.', 'Avinash and Pradeep sir.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3052_3.docx', 'Further plan is to keep the process chamber for pumping and observe its vacuum and pressure.'),
(3294, '2026-01-21 20:33:20', 2457, 'EMT', '4-TEBE, source controller display issue.                                                                                                                              .', '* As observed, the C3 vacuum interlock sensor cable connector\\\'s track was damaged.\\r\\n* Bridge the gap with jumper wire and check the continuity.\\r\\n* Continuity is ok.\\r\\n* Check the source controller with its power unit by attaching its power cable and C2 and C3 sensor cable.\\r\\n* Still Vacuum interlock sensor didn\\\'t activate.\\r\\n* Vinayak sir is communicating with Shirish sir for any suggestions from him.', 'Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3294_2.docx', 'Further troubleshooting is going on with support from Shirish sir (HHV).'),
(3367, '2026-01-22 09:50:37', 2515, 'EMT', 'The CDA line was closed from the ON/OFF regulator. CDA line, vacuum line, and power cord were removed from the PPR AZ Series Spinner. The spinner was shifted from 1.2 Lab to the Nano Litho Lab. CDA line, vacuum line, and power cord were removed from the Nano Litho Lab PPR spinner. The Nano Litho Lab PPR spinner was moved out of the wet bench. The PPR AZ Series Spinner was positioned and retained in the wet bench. CDA line, vacuum line, and power cord were reconnected to the PPR AZ Series Spinner. The Nano Litho Lab PPR spinner shifted 1.2 lab. The PPR Spinner was positioned and retained in the 1.2 lab wet bench. The CDA line, vacuum line, and power cord were reconnected to the PPR Spinner. The CDA line was turned ON from the regulator. The vacuum pump and spinner switch button were turned ON. Functional testing of the 1.2 Lab PPR Spinner was carried out. The spinner is working properly and reaches a vacuum value of 21. Spinner swapping work completed and informed SO Pankaj Sir.', 'The CDA line was closed from the ON/OFF regulator. CDA line, vacuum line, and power cord were removed from the PPR AZ Series Spinner. The spinner was shifted from 1.2 Lab to the Nano Litho Lab. CDA line, vacuum line, and power cord were removed from the Nano Litho Lab PPR spinner. The Nano Litho Lab PPR spinner was moved out of the wet bench. The PPR AZ Series Spinner was positioned and retained in the wet bench. CDA line, vacuum line, and power cord were reconnected to the PPR AZ Series Spinner. The Nano Litho Lab PPR spinner shifted 1.2 lab. The PPR Spinner was positioned and retained in the 1.2 lab wet bench. The CDA line, vacuum line, and power cord were reconnected to the PPR Spinner. The CDA line was turned ON from the regulator. The vacuum pump and spinner switch button were turned ON. Functional testing of the 1.2 Lab PPR Spinner was carried out. The spinner is working properly and reaches a vacuum value of 21. Spinner swapping work completed and informed SO Pankaj Sir.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3367_0.pdf', ''),
(3395, '2026-01-22 09:54:24', 2378, '', 'PIII detail sheet preparation for total slot time calculation with Minita . daily task closing of yesterdays task as it was raised late. email reply to the requests received for process and training request on Proxima. inventory listing of Sirius- above wooden cupboard is ongoing. work updated on HR portal, consumables check and over all DC lab check before leaving.', 'PIII detail sheet preparation for total slot time calculation with Minita . daily task closing of yesterdays task as it was raised late. email reply to the requests received for process and training request on Proxima. inventory listing of Sirius- above wooden cupboard is ongoing. work updated on HR portal, consumables check and over all DC lab check before leaving.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3395_0.docx', '');
