(3560, '2026-01-28 15:56:33', 2457, 'EMT', 'LL vacuum issue, vacuum stuck at 6E-6 torr, it was observed that a small particle is placed on the LL \\\"O\\\" ring.', '1. First, we checked the L.L vacuum and it was stuck to 6.34E-6 torr.\\r\\n2. Then we turned off the L.L MCB, both the turbo pump and rotary pump will turn off simultaneously as both is connected to the same MCB.\\r\\n 3. Removed the power connector from the turbo pump. As the turbo pump and rotary pump is connected to the same MCB.\\r\\n 4. Connected our gauge to the rotary pump\\\'s inlet side and turned on the L.L MCB.\\r\\n 5. Rotary pump started.\\r\\n6. Checked the vacuum at the inlet side and \\r\\n• it was 2.8E-2 mbar in 1 minute.\\r\\n \\r\\n• 7.4E-4 mbar in 2 minutes.\\r\\n \\r\\n• No issue in the rotary pump.\\r\\n7. Connected back the L.L bellow to the Pump\\\'s inlet side and also connected back the exhaust below.\\r\\n 8. Connected back the Turbo’s D-type power connector.\\r\\n 9. As per communication with Vinayak sir it was suggested to clean the “O” ring of the L.L chamber.\\r\\n10. Opened the L.L chamber lid and found one small particle on the \\\"O\\\" ring.\\r\\n 11. Removed the particle and cleaned the \\\"O\\\" with lint-free and IPA.\\r\\n 12.	Close the L.L lid.\\r\\n13.	Cross check all the connections.\\r\\n14.	Turn on the L.L MCB.\\r\\n15.	L.L Vacuum reach from 4.7 torr to 4.98E-6 torr in 9 minutes.\\r\\n16.	Confirmed by Akanksha ji that the vacuum is good.\\r\\n17.	L.L vacuum issue resolved.', 'Avinash, Pradeep sir and Vinayak sir.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3560_0.docx', ''),
(3557, '2026-01-28 16:07:00', 2457, 'EMT', 'LL vacuum issue, vacuum stuck at 6E-6 torr, it was observed that a small particle is placed on the LL \\\"O\\\" ring.', '1. First, we checked the L.L vacuum and it was stuck to 6.34E-6 torr.\\r\\n2. Then we turned off the L.L MCB, both the turbo pump and rotary pump will turn off simultaneously as both is connected to the same MCB.\\r\\n3. Removed the power connector from the turbo pump. As the turbo pump and rotary pump is connected to the same MCB.\\r\\n4. Connected our gauge to the rotary pump&#039;s inlet side and turned on the L.L MCB.\\r\\n5. Rotary pump started.rn6. Checked the vacuum at the inlet side and it was 2.8E-2 mbar in 1 minute and\\r\\n7.4E-4 mbar in 2 minutes and No issue in the rotary pump.\\r\\n8. Connected back the L.L bellow to the Pumps inlet side and also connected back the exhaust below.\\r\\n8. Connected back the Turbos D-type power connector\\r\\n 9. As per communication with Vinayak sir it was suggested to clean the O ring of the L.L chamber.\\r\\n10. Opened the L.L chamber lid and found one small particle on the O ring.\\r\\n11. Removed the particle and cleaned the O with lint-free and IPA.\\r\\n12. Close the L.L lid.\\r\\n13. Cross check all the connections.\\r\\n14. Turn on the L.L MCB.\\r\\n15. L.L Vacuum reach from 4.7 torr to 4.98E-6 torr in 9 minutes.rn16. Confirmed by Akanksha ji that the vacuum is good.rn17. L.L vacuum issue resolved', 'Avinash and Pradeep sir and vinayak sir', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3557_1.docx', ''),
