(3712, '2026-02-02 19:52:09', 2457, 'EMT', 'It was observed that the last user rotated the Z knob of the manipulator to its extreme position i.e. zero position to which it got stuck.', '1.	Removed the WJFMU connector and vacuum line connection from the manipulator no 1.\\r\\n2.	It was observed that the last user rotated the Z knob of the manipulator to its extreme position i.e. zero position to which it got stuck.\\r\\n3.	Tried to lose the upper nut screw of the Z knob but it didn’t move.\\r\\n4.	Then lose the 3 lower nut screw attached to the Z knob lower ring.\\r\\n5.	Take out the whole Z knob and removed the Upper nut screw with Screw driver\\r\\n6.	Then, free the Z knob zero position.\\r\\n7.	Checked it’s working.\\r\\n8.	Cleaned the Z knob whole assembly with dry lint-free.\\r\\n9.	First attached the Upper nut screw of the Z knob and check is working.\\r\\n10.	Placed the Z knob assembly to its position and tighten all the 3 lower nut screw.\\r\\n11.	Check its working and it work fine.\\r\\n12.	Confirmed by SO Shreyasi ji.', 'Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3712_1.docx', ''),
(3787, '2026-02-02 20:26:24', 2457, 'EMT', 'It was observed that the Y axis movement is not working properly.                                                                                 .', '1.	Removed the WJFMU connector and vacuum line connection from the manipulator no 4.\\r\\n2.	It was observed that the Y axis movement is not working properly.\\r\\n3.	When we rotate the Y knob to its extreme position zero, manipulator moves forward and when we strength back the Y knob to its home position manipulator stuck and didn’t move and only Y knob moves.\\r\\n4.	Open the top panel of the manipulator to see any debris that may cause arm to not move back to its home position.\\r\\n5.	Check its movement and it was still getting stuck.\\r\\n6.	Then lose the 3-nut screw of the Z knob circular ring and take out the Z knob assembly as Y-axis arm is attached to Z knob assembly.\\r\\n7.	And try to move the Y axis it was moving but not that much to get it to its home position.\\r\\n8.	Then observed one screw below the Z knob which was connected to the Y axis arm.\\r\\n9.	Lose that one screw a little bit and Y axis arm stared to move smoothly with respective to its Knob.\\r\\n10.	Adjust that one screw.\\r\\n11.	Check the working of the Y axis movement and it move smoothly.\\r\\n12.	SO Debankita ji check the Y- axis movement and confirmed it is working fine', 'Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3787_0.docx', ''),
(3786, '2026-02-02 20:31:12', 2017, 'Safety team', 'Please find attached the Manual Call Point (MCP) images (Images 1-3) that need to be fixed in Lab 7.1 prior to the visit on 05/02/2026. - work done', 'Two manual call points in 7.1 lab and main corridor were fixed today successfully with the help of FSO team.', 'Safety team & FSO team', 'Akshay enterprises', '1196', 'Good', 'NA', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3786_0.pdf', ''),
