(3570, '2026-02-03 22:15:53', 2177, 'Process team', 'The complaint was reviewed and the tool was checked through baseline deposition run. The deposited film was then characterized by dektak for thickness and 4 probe for sheet resistance measurements . All measured parameters were found to be within specified limits.', 'The complaint was reviewed and the tool was checked through baseline deposition run. The deposited film was then characterized by dektak for thickness and 4 probe for sheet resistance measurements . All measured parameters were found to be within specified limits.', 'shahiroze', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3570_1.pptx', ''),
(1458, '2026-02-04 09:59:20', 2457, 'EMT', 'Installation of New VC412 MFC controller received from ultech on 21-01-2026 in PDS tool and manually running the process as per updated SOP.', 'Action Taken: -\\r\\n1.	Received new VC412 MFC controller from Ultech on 21-01-2026.\\r\\n2.	Installed it to PDS system on 29-01-2026.\\r\\n3.	First, we turn off the power of the existing VC412 MFC controller.\\r\\n4.	Removed all the connections i.e. Power cable, grounding wire, MFC’s cable, throttle valve and RS232 com cable connections from the VC412.\\r\\n5.	Installed the new VC412 MFC controller and connected all the cable to its respective label position.\\r\\n6.	Turn on the VC412 MFC controller.\\r\\n7.	Tested its working with software by adjusting the APC position from software and observing its communication with VC412 controller.\\r\\n8.	Started editing the update SOP for manual runs with Pradeep sir via TeamViewer.\\r\\n9.	Done 2 hands on training by manually running the recipe.\\r\\n10.	Before starting the process, Process chamber vacuum was 2.94E-5 torr.\\r\\n11.	First, we run O2 clean recipe manually as per updated SOP,\\r\\nAPC – 10%\\r\\nO2 – 30 sccm\\r\\nSource power – 500 W (FWD)\\r\\nREF – 2 W\\r\\nChamber vacuum – 1.95E-2 Torr\\r\\nTime – 10 minutes\\r\\n12.	Recipe complete successfully.\\r\\n13.	Turned off the source power and set the source power to 0W\\r\\n14.	Set O2 MFC to 0 sccm.\\r\\n15.	Open the APC and waited for chamber vacuum to drop to E-5 Torr.\\r\\n16.	Before starting the process, Process chamber vacuum was 2.94E-5 Torr.\\r\\n17.	Then, we run CHF3 chamber cleaning recipe manually as per from recipe list mention in software i.e. “Chamber_cleaning_01032021_10min”\\r\\nAPC – 30%\\r\\nCHF3 – 20 sccm\\r\\nSource Power(W) – 500\\r\\nBias Power\\r\\nVolt (V) - 200(199-200)\\r\\nFreq (Hz) - 100\\r\\nPulse (uS) - 3\\r\\nTime - 10 minutes \\r\\nChamber Vac - 7.83E-3 - 8.38E-3 torr\\r\\n18.	Recipe complete successfully.\\r\\n19.	Turned off the Bias Power and set the Bias Power to its respective before values.\\r\\n20.	Turned off the source power and set the source power to 0W\\r\\n21.	Close the CHF3 MFC inlet valve and set CHF3 MFC to 0 sccm.\\r\\n22.	Open the APC and waited for chamber vacuum to drop to E-5 torr.\\r\\n23.	Chamber vacuum reaches to 2.93E-5 Torr.', 'Avinash, Pradeep sir', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/1458_16.docx', 'Today Hands On training done and 2 manually recipe run successfully along wit Pradeep sir.\\r\\nRecipes run was\\r\\n1.	O2 clean recipe.\\r\\n2.	CHF3 clean recipe'),
(3474, '2026-02-04 10:07:45', 2515, 'EMT', 'Remove the vacuum gauges connected to the right side of the furnace. Disconnect the rotary pump vacuum line. Loosen and open the glass tube holding plate bolts on both the left and right sides of the furnace. Carefully remove the g lass tube. Remove the cylindrical chamber. Remove the furnace heater and thermocouple from the furnace assembly. Open the furnace base plate bolts and remove the furnace from the CVD bench. Disconnect the controller wire and the thermocouple wire connected to the furnace.', 'Remove the vacuum gauges connected to the right side of the furnace. Disconnect the rotary pump vacuum line. Loosen and open the glass tube holding plate bolts on both the left and right sides of the furnace. Carefully remove the g lass tube. Remove the cylindrical chamber. Remove the furnace heater and thermocouple from the furnace assembly. Open the furnace base plate bolts and remove the furnace from the CVD bench. Disconnect the controller wire and the thermocouple wire connected to the furnace. All dismantled parts are handed over to Sera ji.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad, Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3474_1.pdf', ''),
