(3793, '2026-02-04 14:48:18', 2457, 'EMT', 'CDA pneumatic valve CDA flow issue and Power issue.                                                                                                    .', 'Action Taken: - CDA flow issue and power supply issue in CDA pneumatic manifold assembly\\r\\nICPRIE New update (03-02-2026).\\r\\n1. CDA flow is now coming to the CDA pneumatic inlet side of the CDA manifold, as we press and hold the Festo R/O-3-PK-3 roller lever pneumatic valve interlock sensor which is on the Gas panel door.\\r\\n2. But due to no power in the CDA pneumatic manifold assembly/solenoid valve, CDA is not passing to other lines i.e. VGQ0, VGQ1, ....\\r\\n3. Without power supply in CDA pneumatic manifold we are able to open the VGQ values through software but due to no CDA manifold is not operatable.\\r\\n4. So, we trace the power cable of the CDA pneumatic manifold assembly and it is going/connected to the WAGO Plc module Port 3.2 - Port 3.5.     \\r\\n5. Also, it was observed that some of the PVC Insulated wires are cut.\\r\\n6. To confirm we need a pin diagram of the 25 pin CDA pneumatic manifold power cable coming from the WAGO Plc module to pneumatic manifold assembly.\\r\\n\\r\\nNote: -\\r\\n• DGB solenoid valve is the same valve which carry forwards the CDA flow to CDA PNEUMATIC MANIFOLD ASSEMBLY and it is getting 22.80vdc which is coming and connected to the WAGO Plc module port 3.6.\\r\\n • In the WAGO Plc module from Port 3.2 - Port 3.5 it has PVC insulated wires which are going/connected to the CDA manifold power cable. We need pin diagram of the 25-pin connector to verify if supply is getting or not', 'Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3793_0.docx', ''),
(3052, '2026-02-04 15:00:45', 2457, 'EMT', 'CDA pneumatic valve CDA flow issue and Power issue.                                                                                             .', 'Action Taken: - Gas box pneumatic valves check troubleshooting.\\r\\n\\r\\nSummary: - We have checked the gas line till the high-pressure diaphragm valve (final valve) and no leak is observed in the line.\\r\\n\\r\\nFurther troubleshooting: - \\r\\n1. In previous troubleshooting when we try to open the VGQ valve it didn’t open as turbo pump was off.\\r\\n2. Opened the rough valve (VVV) and open the throttle valve 100% position.\\r\\n3. Open the PN2 valve and turn ON the turbo pump.\\r\\nTurbo speed – 630 Hz\\r\\nCurrent – 1.14A\\r\\nPenning gauge – 1.48E-5mbar\\r\\nMVV – 14.1Pa\\r\\n4. Close the throttle valve to 30% position.\\r\\nPenning gauge – 1.52E-5mbar\\r\\nMVV – 14.0Pa\\r\\n5. Open the VGQ valve and also open the VGQ1 and VGQ2.\\r\\n6. No change seen in chamber vacuum and in pressure i.e. penning gauge and MVV gauge.\\r\\n7. Also, while opening the VGQ valve no sound hear as usual it should come while opening the VGQ valve.\\r\\n8. So next, we check that CDA flow is coming from the VGQ valve when we open it from software, (i.e. remove the CDA line from the VGQ valve and open the VGQ valve from the software and see if the CDA flow is coming or not.)\\r\\n9. Closed the VGQ1 and VGQ2 valve and also close the VGQ valve.\\r\\n10. Disconnected the CDA line from VGQ valve.\\r\\n11. Open the VGQ valve from the software to check CDA is coming from the VGQ line or not\\r\\n12. No CDA flow came from the VGQ line.\\r\\n13. To cross check, disconnected the CDA line from the VGQ1 valve also and open the VGQ1 valve from the software.\\r\\n14. No CDA flow in VGQ1 line also.\\r\\n\\r\\nSuspects: -\\r\\n• No power in the CDA pneumatic manifold assembly observed.\\r\\n \\r\\n• No CDA flow in the CDA pneumatic manifold to which it is not passing CDA pressure to other connecting lines.', 'Avinash (EMT).', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3052_4.docx', ''),
(3052, '2026-02-04 15:03:27', 2457, 'EMT', 'CDA pneumatic valve CDA flow issue and Power issue.                                                                                .', 'Action Taken: - CDA flow issue and power supply issue in CDA pneumatic manifold assemblyrnICPRIE New update (03-02-2026).rn1. CDA flow is now coming to the CDA pneumatic inlet side of the CDA manifold, as we press and hold the Festo R/O-3-PK-3 roller lever pneumatic valve interlock sensor which is on the Gas panel door.rn2. But due to no power in the CDA pneumatic manifold assembly/solenoid valve, CDA is not passing to other lines i.e. VGQ0, VGQ1, ....rn3. Without power supply in CDA pneumatic manifold we are able to open the VGQ values through software but due to no CDA manifold is not operatable.rn4. So, we trace the power cable of the CDA pneumatic manifold assembly and it is going/connected to the WAGO Plc module Port 3.2 - Port 3.5. rn5. Also, it was observed that some of the PVC Insulated wires are cut.rn6. To confirm we need a pin diagram of the 25 pin CDA pneumatic manifold power cable coming from the WAGO Plc module to pneumatic manifold assembly.rnrnNote: -rn&bull; DGB solenoid valve is the same valve which carry forwards the CDA flow to CDA PNEUMATIC MANIFOLD ASSEMBLY and it is getting 22.80vdc which is coming and connected to the WAGO Plc module port 3.6.rn &bull; In the WAGO Plc module from Port 3.2 - Port 3.5 it has PVC insulated wires which are going/connected to the CDA manifold power cable. We need pin diagram of the 25-pin connector to verify if supply is getting or not', 'Avinash (EMT).', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3052_5.docx', 'mail has been sent to Lab India engineer Mr. Sachin shette ji regarding issue.'),
(3754, '2026-02-04 15:17:58', 189, 'Process team', 'Baseline run for the month of Feb to check system health and baseline performance                   .', 'Baseline run performed for the following:\\r\\n Al2O3 thermal at 200deg for 100cycles in ALD Non LL tool.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
