(3810, '2026-02-04 15:25:09', 189, 'Process team', 'Process meeting                                                                                                .', 'completed                                                                                                         .', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(3257, '2026-02-04 15:29:05', 2495, 'EMT', 'Water flowing continuously from nano DI plant                                                                  .', 'To resolve the issue permanently, the solenoid valve and PCB were bypassed using an external button. After reinstallation, the dispenser was tested and found to be working properly with no leakage. The top dispenser button was sealed securely, and the dispenser was reattached. An email will be sent instructing users not to press or tamper with the top dispenser button. Please refer to the Report attached for further details and pictures', 'Rhifa, Mandar', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3257_3.docx', ''),
(3778, '2026-02-04 15:38:35', 189, 'Process', 'removing sample from lift off and microscopic imaging                                               .', 'Voyager baseline sample removed from PG remover after overnight lift off and did the microscopic imaging to check the patterns.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(1868, '2026-02-04 15:48:35', 2495, 'EMT', 'Installation of the High Magnification Optical Microscope in IITBNF lab                                                                                        .', 'The engineer arrived and delivered the package at 9:00 AM on 8th January 2026. After unboxing, the microscope was shifted to the Nano-2 Lab for installation.\\r\\nThe engineer then started the assembly of the microscope. Switch board connection was done by facility team. A computer and CPU were brought from the office for the microscope installation. The microscope was connected to the PC, and the required software was downloaded and installed on the system.\\r\\nAfter software installation, the engineer carried out the calibration of the microscope. Once the calibration process was completed, the engineer provided a detailed explanation of the microscope operation and usage procedure to the process team( Pankaj sir, Shilpa mam). Please refer to the below attached report for further details and pictures', 'Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/1868_17.pdf', ''),
(3825, '2026-02-04 16:03:09', 2495, 'EMT', 'DI water tank of Nano Litho service corridor needs to be refilled every week starting from today                                         .', 'With help of Housekeeping staff filled the Tank by using 20 liter water can and filled it with di water from wet chemistry lab', 'Rhifa', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(3843, '2026-02-04 16:45:19', 279, 'EMT', 'Precursor change.                                           \\r\\n                                   .           \\r\\n.                        .', 'Ti precursor head space purge done.\\r\\nTi precursor replaced with TMA precursor with new VCR gasket.\\r\\nTMA precursor head space purge done.', 'Vinayak', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(3855, '2026-02-04 16:48:41', 189, 'Process team', 'Voyager tool turning ON after it was turned off last night due to power issue in the lab                          .', 'Tool turned ON as per the Standard operating procedure and now waiting the beam to get stabilized and achieve the vacuum', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3855_0.docx', ''),
(3798, '2026-02-04 17:02:00', 89, 'EMT, Process', 'Checked the system and found the alignment cross hair line (+) was not stable due to which software did not move further', 'After talking to Shubhankar, the previous user had done glass sample. Due to the difference in the thickness of glass substrate and Si wafer, the stage X-Y adjustment was required.\\r\\n\\r\\nDid the X-Y stage adjustment to align the sample so that the beam is aligned. In the software the cross hair is stable and aligned at the center\\r\\n\\r\\nSiO2 standard sample measurement was done\\r\\nAnother sample of ALD HfO2 measurement was done\\r\\n\\r\\nBoth the runs completed successfully', 'Pradeep, Shubhankar', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
