(3831, '2026-02-04 19:34:39', 2457, 'EMT', 'Sample fell off during the process, need to open the bottom panel to check the location of sample...', 'Action Taken: - \\r\\n1. SO Nihal Raut vented the chamber.\\r\\n2. Opened the chamber to inspect the fallen sample wafer inside the chamber.\\r\\n3. No sample seen in the chamber.\\r\\n4. Turn off the rotary scroll pump.\\r\\n5. Remove the SS below from the Pump’s inlet side.\\r\\n6. It was found that the pump’s inlet filter was cover with broken small particles of the wafer.\\r\\n 7. Removed the Circlip Plier from the filter and take out the filter.\\r\\n 8. Removed all the small particles and clean the filter.\\r\\n 9. Also cleaned the minor particles inside of the pump’s inlet side with vacuum cleaner.\\r\\n10. Placed the filter back to pump’s inlet and attached the Circlip.\\r\\n11. Connected back the SS bellow to pump’s inlet side.\\r\\n12. Turn on the rotary scroll pump.\\r\\n13. SO Nihal Raut pump down the chamber.\\r\\n14. Run one O2 clean recipe i.e. “Aakash_300C_O2_2mins”\\r\\n15. Tool functioning properly.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3831_1.docx', 'Sample broken and small pieces of the sample were removed from the pump’s inlet filter.\\r\\nRotary pump working fine, one baseline runs carried out by SO Nihal Raut.'),
(3842, '2026-02-04 19:36:08', 2457, 'EMT', 'Sample fell off during the process, need to open the bottom panel to check the location of sample...', 'Action Taken: -\\r\\n1. SO Nihal Raut vented the chamber.\\r\\n2. Opened the chamber to inspect the fallen sample wafer inside the chamber.\\r\\n3. No sample seen in the chamber.\\r\\n4. Turn off the rotary scroll pump.\\r\\n5. Remove the SS below from the Pump’s inlet side.\\r\\n6. It was found that the pump’s inlet filter was cover with broken small particles of the wafer.\\r\\n7. Removed the Circlip Plier from the filter and take out the filter.\\r\\n8. Removed all the small particles and clean the filter.\\r\\n9. Also cleaned the minor particles inside of the pump’s inlet side with vacuum cleaner.\\r\\n10. Placed the filter back to pump’s inlet and attached the Circlip.\\r\\n11. Connected back the SS bellow to pump’s inlet side.\\r\\n12. Turn on the rotary scroll pump.\\r\\n13. SO Nihal Raut pump down the chamber.\\r\\n14. Run one O2 clean recipe i.e. “Aakash_300C_O2_2mins”\\r\\n15. Tool functioning properly.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3842_0.docx', 'Sample broken and small pieces of the sample were removed from the pump’s inlet filter.\\r\\nRotary pump working fine, one baseline runs carried out by SO Nihal Raut.'),
(3744, '2026-02-04 19:40:32', 928, '', 'Lab Cleaning, Tools cleaning, Consumable, chemical, and resist check for Nano Litho lab is done successfully.', 'Lab Cleaning, Tools cleaning, Consumable, chemical, and resist check for Nano Litho lab is done successfully.', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3744_0.pdf', ''),
(3830, '2026-02-04 20:16:42', 2457, 'EMT', 'Hands ON training and Manually runs as per updated.                                                                                                            .', 'Action Taken: - Manual test run as per updated SOP.\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Sample wafer was in Process chamber after the previous test runs.\\r\\n2. Loaded the sample wafer back to Load Lock (L.L) chamber as per SOP.\\r\\n3. Vented the L.L chamber.\\r\\n4 Removed the sample wafer.\\r\\n5. Cleaned the Sample wafer with lint-free cloth and IPA\\r\\n6. Also use N2 gun on sample wafer to removed any leftover dry particles.\\r\\n7. Placed the sample wafer back to L.L chamber.\\r\\n8. Put the L.L chamber into Low Vac.\\r\\n9. Low Vac completed.\\r\\n10. Closed the Gate valve and open the slit valve.\\r\\n11. Transfer the Sample wafer to Process chamber manually as per updated SOP.\\r\\n12. Closed the slit valve and open the gate valve.\\r\\n13. Ran “O2 gas test_23012020” recipe manually i.e. all the parameters set manually.\\r\\nAPC -10%\\r\\nO2 - 30 sccm\\r\\nSource Power(W) – 500\\r\\nBias Power\\r\\nVolt (V) – 4000\\r\\nFreq (Hz) – 200\\r\\nPulse (uS) – 5\\r\\nChamber vacuum - 8.65E-3 Torr\\r\\nTime - 10min\\r\\n 14. 1 run completed as per updated SOP from start to end.\\r\\n15. Did pump-purge cycle 5 times in the process chamber.\\r\\n16. Unloaded the sample to L.L chamber.\\r\\n17. Did pump-purge cycle 5 times in the L.L chamber before opening the L.L chamber', 'Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3830_0.docx', '1 run completed as per updated SOP from start to end.'),
(1458, '2026-02-04 20:18:33', 2457, 'EMT', 'Hands ON training and Manually runs as per updated.                                                                                        .', 'Action Taken: - Manual test run as per updated SOP.\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Sample wafer was in Process chamber after the previous test runs.\\r\\n2. Loaded the sample wafer back to Load Lock (L.L) chamber as per SOP.\\r\\n3. Vented the L.L chamber.\\r\\n4 Removed the sample wafer.\\r\\n5. Cleaned the Sample wafer with lint-free cloth and IPA\\r\\n6. Also use N2 gun on sample wafer to removed any leftover dry particles.\\r\\n7. Placed the sample wafer back to L.L chamber.\\r\\n8. Put the L.L chamber into Low Vac.\\r\\n9. Low Vac completed.\\r\\n10. Closed the Gate valve and open the slit valve.\\r\\n11. Transfer the Sample wafer to Process chamber manually as per updated SOP.\\r\\n12. Closed the slit valve and open the gate valve.\\r\\n13. Ran “O2 gas test_23012020” recipe manually i.e. all the parameters set manually.\\r\\nAPC -10%\\r\\nO2 - 30 sccm\\r\\nSource Power(W) – 500\\r\\nBias Power\\r\\nVolt (V) – 4000\\r\\nFreq (Hz) – 200\\r\\nPulse (uS) – 5\\r\\nChamber vacuum - 8.65E-3 Torr\\r\\nTime - 10min\\r\\n14. 1 run completed as per updated SOP from start to end.\\r\\n15. Did pump-purge cycle 5 times in the process chamber.\\r\\n16. Unloaded the sample to L.L chamber.\\r\\n17. Did pump-purge cycle 5 times in the L.L chamber before opening the L.L chamber', 'Avinash', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/1458_17.docx', '1 run completed as per updated SOP from start to end.'),
