(1521, '2026-02-06 15:52:13', 297, 'AHU Chiller Team', 'Discussion with prof. AT on 5th Feb along with Abhishek, prashant, Pawan, Abhay.\\r\\nDecided to shift PPMS to spintronics lab toward the AC. Measurement taken and tool can be fix in the room.\\r\\nNeed Ramp to take the tool via door of PPMS to Spintronics lab', 'Terrace will be affected or not\\r\\n1.Confirmation from estate weather terrace will get affected or not\\r\\nA.	If No then chiller can be retain in the current position on concrete platform \\r\\nB	If Yes then we need to do following things-\\r\\n2a. Concrete platform for chiller base near enter door of terrace\\r\\n  b.  Move the Hexon chiller on platform with chiller base with Mathadi\\r\\n c. Move the old chiller from the terrace\\r\\n3.Electrical connection 3 phase in spintronics lab from DB \\r\\nMount Remote panel\\r\\n4.Chiller water line laying work - as per ppt ( few material needs to be procured since length has increased)\\r\\n5. Mounting of Chiller Manifold inside lab\\r\\n6. Power termination both chiller side and Remote panel side\\r\\n7. Termination of water lines at chiller and Manifold side\\r\\n8. water top up\\r\\n9. test run \\r\\n10. observation\\r\\n11. Shed for chiller', 'Prashant', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''),
(3895, '2026-02-06 16:26:21', 2495, 'EMT', 'Student complained that Hot plate for DSA is not turning ON                                                          .', 'The hot plate was transported from the Nano Lithography Lab to the BMS room for inspection.\\r\\nContinuity of the power cord was checked using a multimeter and found to be in proper working condition.\\r\\nThe fuse was inspected, and it was observed that one of the two 6A fuses was blown. The faulty fuse was replaced with a new 6A fuse.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter replacing the fuse, the hot plate was powered on; however, it still did not operate.\\r\\nThe rear panel of the hot plate was then opened for further inspection.\\r\\n\\r\\nUpon inspection, the Corocom PS0SSDS30 EMI/RFI power entry module was found to be faulty.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe defective module was replaced with a spare Corocom PS0SSDS60 EMI/RFI power entry module taken from a spare hot plate.\\r\\nThe rear panel was closed and secured properly, after which the hot plate was powered on and found to be operational.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe hot plate performance was verified using an external thermocouple, and it was confirmed to be functioning correctly.\\r\\nThe hot plate was returned to the Nano Lithography Lab, where the SO verified and confirmed its proper operation.\\r\\nA purchase request was made via email and a sample was given for Corocom PS0SSDS30 EMI/RFI power entry module.', 'Rhifa, Vinayak', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3895_0.pdf', ''),
(3256, '2026-02-06 16:53:15', 2515, 'EMT', 'While rotating the substrate shutter, we observed that the shutter was loose and misaligned. We also noticed that the shutter rotator was rotating beyond its required range.', 'The chamber was vented and the chamber lid was opened. The rotator rotation limit was identified and marked. The shutter was then realigned, and the bolt was tightened. The substrate shutter open/close issue was resolved. Inform SO Minita mam for using the tool.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/3256_3.pdf', ''),
(2445, '2026-02-06 17:05:13', 2515, 'EMT', 'Turn ON the Rotary pump pump and wait reaching vacuum - 5.0E-2mbar, vacuum reaching time 25 minutes. Then set the combination valve from roughing to backing position. High vacuum reach 5.4E-6mbar in 7 hours 30 minutes.', 'Turn ON the Rotary pump pump and wait reaching vacuum - 5.0E-2mbar (vacuum reaching time 25 minutes). Then set the combination valve from roughing to backing position. High vacuum reach 5.4E-6mbar 7 hours 30 minutes.', 'Vikas Kumar Nishad, Minita mam (SO)', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'uploads/2445_4.pdf', ''),
